1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000
You:  "Brrr...!"

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
*I stare at the road before me, which is now barely visible thanks to the flurry of snow.*

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
*The storm had arrived violently while I was out, and before I knew it, I had gotten stuck in the middle of it.*

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,000
You:  "Almost home..."

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
*My breath is visible in front of me as I creep forward on the snowed over road.*

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
*Even though my heater is on full blast - it isn't enough to ward off the freezing cold.*

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
*I shudder to think of how cold I'd be without it.*

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
*(The sooner I get home, the better. I'd hate to get stranded out here in this.)*

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:41,000
*Slowing my truck to a stop in front of the cabin, I turn the key in the ignition and shut it off.*

10
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,000
*The heater immediately stops blowing, and I can already feel the chill hit me.*

11
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,000
*Time to brace myself for the freezing winds raging between me and the cabin.*

12
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,000
You:  "Here goes..."

13
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
*I rush inside as quickly as I can, shivering from head to toe despite my thick clothing.*

14
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:07,000
*The moment I slam the door shut behind me, the sound of the wind howling outside quietens, and the chattering of my teeth fills the room.*

15
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:15,000
*It's warmer in here, but not to the point where I can whimsically toss aside my extra layers and flop down on the couch.*

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:23,000
*If I suddenly remove all of my extra layers right this instant, I'll probably pass out from the change in temperature.*

17
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,000
You:  "Whose idea was it to start living out here anyway?"

18
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,000
*As the sole occupant of this cabin, I expect no response to my rhetorical question.*

19
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:40,000
*For better or worse, I decided for myself that I would live in these snowy mountains, all on my own.*

20
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
You:  "Alright. Tea, a bite to eat, and then I'll turn in for the night."

21
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:51,000
You:  "In the middle of a snowstorm like this, it's important to keep nourished and warm."

22
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:58,000
*After reminding myself to adhere to a few basic survival tips, I fill the kettle with water and turn it on.*

23
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
You:  "Man, am I glad I have electricity out here."

24
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:07,000
You:  "Without ready access to hot water, there's no way that I'd survive out here."

25
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:16,000
You:  "I should have enough food to last until Summer too, by which point I'll be able to go into town without freezing to death."

26
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,000
You:  "Life out here might just work out after all."

27
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,000
*The moment I think so, my body begins to shiver once more.*

28
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:31,000
*I feel cold wind brush up against my cheek, threatening to give me frostbite if I dare to take off any layers of clothing.*

29
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:36,000
You:  "Th-That's weird. It shouldn't be th-this cold inside the cabin."

30
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:45,000
You:  "I know there's a snowstorm out there, but this cabin is pretty well-insulated. It shouldn't be this cold unless the door is open."

31
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:54,000
*Curious about the source, and also desperate to stop the cold, I walk through the cabin, trying to figure out where it's coming from.*

32
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:00,000
*After checking all of the windows, I wind up near the back entrance of the cabin.*

33
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:05,000
*And surely enough, as soon as I spot the back door, I have my answer.*

34
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,000
You:  "Aha! Gotcha."

35
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:15,000
*I hurriedly clear away the snow at the base of the door, which seems to have stopped the door from opening or closing any further.*

36
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:24,000
*I then close the door, lock it, and move a few things in front of the door to prevent it from opening even if the lock were to break.*

37
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
You:  "That ought to do it."

38
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:30,000
You:  "But how did the door get open in the first place?"

39
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:38,000
*I could see myself forgetting to lock it, since I'm all alone out here anyway, but there's no way I'd forget to close it.*

40
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
You:  "Is the latch broken...?"

41
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:46,000
You:  "{i}sigh...{/i} Forget it. I'll think about it after I've had something warm to drink."

42
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:50,000
*I turn away from the door and begin to walk towards the kitchen.*

43
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:56,000
*No sooner have I begun to move my foot, however, than I realize that the floor is soaking wet.*

44
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:00,000
You:  "Ah... Some snow must have blown in and melted."

45
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,000
You:  "I guess I'd better clean this..."

46
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,000
You:  "...Up?"

47
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,000
*My eyes widen as I realize something important.*

48
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:11,000
*There isn't just one puddle of water; there are several.*

49
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:18,000
*Following a clear, non-linear path, the puddles show me the path someone, or some{i}thing{/i}, has taken.*

50
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
You:  "Damn. An intruder? Or maybe a wild animal?"

51
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:26,000
*I instinctively grab an axe that I keep for wood off the back wall.*

52
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:36,000
*Axe in hand, I head deeper into the storeroom, prepared to defend myself against the potentially dangerous person or animal that has wandered into my home.*

53
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:41,000
*Moving even further inside, I cautiously move around the table and-*

54
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,000
*...Freeze.*

55
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Mirari:  "{i}haa... haa... haa... *shiver*{/i}"

56
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,000
You:  "What the..."

57
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:51,000
*My arms lose all strength as I stare at the peculiar sight in front of me.*

58
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
*On the floor in my storeroom is a girl.*

59
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
*She's shivering, wet, and her breath is ragged.*

60
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:04,000
*Red-faced, yet blue in the fingertips, the poor girl looks like she's about to freeze to death at any moment.*

61
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,000
*And yet, what attracts my attention is--*

62
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,000
You:  "That tail... and those ears..."

63
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
You:  "It couldn't be..."

64
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:18,000
*Without thinking, I drop my axe on the floor and reach out towards the girl's ears.*

65
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:24,000
*I gently tug on her ears, trying to pull them off, or otherwise expose their stitching.*

66
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:30,000
*However, no matter how hard I pull, there is no sign of it being a practical joke.*

67
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:34,000
*As far as I can tell, these wolf-like ears are real.*

68
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
You:  "Impossible... She really is a half-human?"

69
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:45,000
You:  "That can't be right. I made absolutely certain that this place wasn't intruding on the domain of any half-humans."

70
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,000
You:  "Did I make a mistake? Or is she just--"

71
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Mirari:  "Nnngg... {i}*shiver*{/i}"

72
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:56,000
*Before I can mull over the girl's presence any further, her whimper brings me back to reality.*

73
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:04,000
You:  "Right. Whatever the reason for her presence here, it doesn't change the fact that she's freezing to death in my cabin."

74
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:10,000
You:  "I'll worry about the details later. For now, I have to make sure she doesn't die."

75
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:17,000
*I grab a towel from one of the shelves in the storeroom and immediately begin to dry the young girl off.*

76
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:23,000
*The moment I make contact with her skin, I realize just how close to death this girl really is.*

77
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:31,000
*Her body is so cold that I can feel it through the towel. Her skin is deathly pale, and she can't stop shivering.*

78
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:36,000
*Desperately, I rub the girl's body, trying to both dry her off and warm her up.*

79
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:41,000
*However, no matter how much her body moves about, she does not stir.*

80
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:48,000
*The girl is breathing, but unconscious. Even if I tried to, I don't think I'd be able to wake her up.*

81
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
You:  "...Shit. This isn't working."

82
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,000
You:  "I'm going to have to step things up a notch."

83
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:58,000
*Many hours pass by as the unconscious wolf-girl continues to rest.*

84
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:04,000
*Over time, her breathing gradually becomes less ragged, and color returns to her skin.*

85
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:12,000
*The incessant shivering comes to an end, her lips stop quivering, and a faint yet peaceful smile appears on her face.*

86
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:18,000
*While it's still too soon to rest easy, it seems like the girl is going to be just fine.*

87
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:24,000
You:  "Phew. I was worried for a while there, but it looks like things have finally calmed down."

88
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:30,000
You:  "I guess some dry clothes and a long sleep in a warm cabin were all she needed."

89
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:39,000
*Feeling good about myself for having been able to help out, I watch the girl sleep for a while as I contemplate what to do next.*

90
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:46,000
You:  "The snowstorm has died down now, so I should probably have this girl leave as soon as she wakes up."

91
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:55,000
You:  "...Though, I suppose I could at least feed her first. She must be famished after sleeping for so long, and almost freezing to death."

92
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:59,000
You:  "It would be heartless for me to not at least--"

93
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
Mirari:  "{i}*groan*{/i} Mmm..."

94
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:07,000
*While I'm in the middle of thinking out loud, the wolf-girl finally begins to move.*

95
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:13,000
*What starts out as a faint groan quickly turns into visible movement on her part.*

96
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:17,000
*The girl's eyelids twitch, and I can see her lips trembling.*

97
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:21,000
*In a matter of seconds, she will no doubt open her eyes.*

98
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
Mirari:  "Mmm... {i}*yawn*{/i}"

99
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Mirari:  "That was quite a--"

100
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Mirari:  "...Eh?"

101
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:30,000
*The girl's eyes open wide as she starts to gain her bearings.*

102
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:35,000
*Her eyes dart around the room, trying to fill in the blanks of her memory.*

103
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Mirari:  "Oh... Yes. I remember now."

104
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Mirari:  "I got caught up in the snowstorm, didn't I?"

105
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Mirari:  "I finally found shelter, but... I thought my mind was just playing tricks on me as my body started to shut down."

106
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,000
Mirari:  "Am I really... alive?"

107
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:55,000
You:  "You sure are. At least, as far as I can tell."

108
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Mirari:  "Uwah!!?"

109
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:00,000
*The girl jumps in fright as she finally notices my presence.*

110
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Mirari:  "Y-You are-- U-Uhm, this is...!!"

111
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:08,000
*The girl tries to speak, but fails to formulate a proper sentence.*

112
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:15,000
*With that being the case, I decide to explain the situation to her, giving her time to calm down.*

113
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:20,000
You:  "I found you in my storeroom, shivering and unconscious on the floor."

114
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:27,000
You:  "I dried you off and brought you inside, but it was hard to tell if you were going to survive or not."

115
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:35,000
You:  "Your fingertips had already started to turn blue by the time I found you, and your breathing was a complete mess."

116
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:39,000
*Listening to my calm explanation, the girl looks down at herself.*

117
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:44,000
*She pinches her clothing, seemingly surprised at how clean and dry they are.*

118
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Mirari:  "My... My clothes..."

119
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,000
Mirari:  "Did you...?"

120
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,000
*I avert my gaze.*

121
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,000
You:  "Ah... Yeah, I did."

122
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:57,000
You:  "Your clothes were wet, and you were at risk of freezing to death. I couldn't just leave you like that."

123
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,000
*Just like me, the girl blushes and looks away.*

124
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:04,000
*Rather than adopt an expression of anger, however--*

125
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Mirari:  "...Thank you."

126
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,000
You:  "...Huh?"

127
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:10,000
*The girl forces herself to look at me once more.*

128
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:14,000
*With eyes filled with sincerity, she continues to speak.*

129
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Mirari:  "I... I am a trespasser."

130
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:23,000
Mirari:  "I broke into your cabin, intruded in your home, and dared to use your shelter as my own."

131
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:28,000
Mirari:  "Yet, despite all of that, you went to such lengths for me..."

132
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:32,000
You:  "Oh... Yeah, I guess you could look at it that way."

133
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:42,000
You:  "It really isn't that big of a deal though. You were caught in the middle of a snowstorm; if I were in your situation, I would have broken in, too."

134
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:48,000
You:  "Besides, all I did was dry you off and clean your clothes. It's really nothing major."

135
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Mirari:  "It {i}is{/i} something major!"

136
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:55,000
Mirari:  "If you hadn't taken pity on me, I would have...!"

137
00:10:55,000 --> 00:11:01,000
*Before the girl can finish speaking, she's interrupted by the sound of the kettle whistling.*

138
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,000
You:  "Ah, it sounds like breakfast is ready."

139
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
You:  "Excuse me for a moment."

140
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:10,000
*I move away from the girl and head towards the kitchen.*

141
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:18,000
*Once I set foot in front of the kettle, I grab an additional ceramic bowl for my guest, since she has now woken up.*

142
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Mirari:  "B... Breakfast...?"

143
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Mirari:  "You mean to say that... it is now morning?"

144
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:28,000
You:  "That's right. You were asleep for a solid twelve hours."

145
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:34,000
*After emptying two packets of instant noodles, one into each bowl, I pour in the boiling water.*

146
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:42,000
*I then place a fork in each bowl and bring them back into the living room, careful not to let the water spill over the sides.*

147
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
You:  "Alright, here you go."

148
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:49,000
You:  "Make sure to give it a few minutes to cook before you eat it."

149
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:55,000
*As I set a bowl down on the table in front of the girl, she stares at it quizzically.*

150
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Mirari:  "Eat... this?"

151
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Mirari:  "What is this? Some kind of soup?"

152
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:03,000
You:  "Kind of. They're instant noodles."

153
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:10,000
You:  "All you need to do is put the noodles in a bowl, add hot water, then wait for a couple of minutes."

154
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,000
You:  "They're quick, easy, warm, and quite tasty."

155
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:17,000
*I begin to stir my noodles around with my fork as I speak.*

156
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:25,000
*Watching me carefully, the girl hesitantly picks up her fork, stares at it for a moment, then mimics my action.*

157
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:28,000
You:  "Yeah, that's good. Just like that."

158
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:34,000
You:  "You've gotta stir them up a little so that the flavoring is distributed evenly."

159
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Mirari:  "The... flavoring?"

160
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:40,000
You:  "It adds additional flavor to the otherwise bland noodles."

161
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:43,000
You:  "Have you ever eaten instant food before?"

162
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,000
*The girl shakes her head.*

163
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:53,000
Mirari:  "I'm familiar with many aspects of human culture, including some which our respective races do not share."

164
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:57,000
Mirari:  "Even so, instant food is an entirely new concept to me."

165
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
You:  "Is... Is that right...?"

166
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:05,000
*I stare at the girl in partial surprise as she responds with unexpected eloquence.*

167
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:12,000
*Far from my mental image of half-humans being savages, this girl seems to be more human than wolf.*

168
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:16,000
Mirari:  "...Oh my goodness! I just realized something!"

169
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Mirari:  "I've been preying on your kindness, yet I haven't even given my name, or asked for yours!"

170
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:26,000
You:  "Oh... Yeah. I guess you're right."

171
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:31,000
You:  "It doesn't really matter though. It's not like you'll be staying--"

172
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Mirari:  "I am Mirari!"

173
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:44,000
Mirari:  "My pack resides on the other side of this mountain. I was away from the pack when the snowstorm hit, and I wound up being unable to return to them."

174
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:47,000
Mirari:  "Thank you again for taking care of me!"

175
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:53,000
*Speaking almost too quickly for me to understand her, Mirari introduces herself in a panic.*

176
00:13:53,000 --> 00:14:00,000
*She takes a few quick breaths immediately afterwards, then finally begins to calm down once again.*

177
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:03,000
You:  "Uhm... Pleased to meet you, Mirari."

178
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:08,000
You:  "My name is [player_name]. I've been living in this cabin by myself for--"

179
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Mirari:  "[player_name]!"

180
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,000
You:  "Y-Yes!?"

181
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:16,000
Mirari:  "[player_name]. [player_name], [player_name], [player_name]."

182
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Mirari:  "...Okay, that ought to do it."

183
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
You:  "Do... what, exactly?"

184
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Mirari:  "Hmm?"

185
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Mirari:  "Oh, my apologies! I didn't mean to interrupt."

186
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Mirari:  "Human names all sound so strange to me. If I don't repeat them out loud, they're too difficult to remember."

187
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,000
You:  "Oh... I see."

188
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,000
You:  "Anyway, Mirari--"

189
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,000
Mirari:  "Yes, [player_name]!?"

190
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,000
You:  "...I think it's ready now."

191
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Mirari:  "...Huh?"

192
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
*I glance down at our food.*

193
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:53,000
*The noodles have begun to expand after absorbing some of the water, and the steam rising from the bowls has lessened considerably.*

194
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:56,000
*If we're going to eat our fill, now is the time.*

195
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
Mirari:  "Oh... Y-Yes. Of course."

196
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Mirari:  "...Uhm..."

197
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:03,000
*Mirari picks up her fork and takes another look at the bowl.*

198
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:11,000
*She raises her fork out of the bowl and licks the water off it, as though she was trying to eat soup with a fork.*

199
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:15,000
*After watching Mirari do this a couple of times, I interrupt her.*

200
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:20,000
You:  "You can drink the water last, after you've eaten all of the noodles."

201
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:23,000
You:  "Just watch me and do what I do."

202
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:26,000
*Under Mirari's watchful gaze, I pick up my fork.*

203
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:33,000
*After pushing it into a clump of noodles and turning the fork a few times, I raise my fork to my mouth.*

204
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:38,000
*I take a big mouthful and happily begin to chew the warm, filling noodles.*

205
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Mirari:  "I-I see... The food is submerged, and the water is too hot to touch, so you use a tool to bring the food to your mouth."

206
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:50,000
You:  "Mmm... {i}*munch*{/i} Pretty much."

207
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:53,000
You:  "Now, why don't you give it a try?"

208
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Mirari:  "Eh!? M-Me!?"

209
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:58,000
You:  "Of course. That's why you were watching me, remember?"

210
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:05,000
You:  "Don't worry, it's dead simple. Just get some noodles on the end of the fork and bring it to your mouth."

211
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
Mirari:  "...O... Okay..."

212
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
Mirari:  "I'll... give it a try."

213
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:12,000
*Mirari nervously picks up her fork once more.*

214
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:19,000
*Mimicking my actions to the best of her ability, Mirari clumsily scoops up a large number of noodles.*

215
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:27,000
*She then raises her utensil, at which point most of the noodles slip off her fork and fall back into the bowl beneath.*

216
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:40,000
*Luckily for Mirari, however, a couple of noodles manage to hang on to the utensil, and after quickly examining the foreign food one more time, Mirari hesitantly places them in her mouth.*

217
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Mirari:  "Mmm!?"

218
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,000
You:  "Is it good?"

219
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Mirari:  "This... This is..."

220
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:48,000
Mirari:  "This is delicious! It's absolutely amazing!"

221
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:53,000
Mirari:  "How can something this tasty be cooked in such a short period of time?"

222
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:55,000
Mirari:  "Ah... The snowstorm."

223
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
Mirari:  "...I hope she's alright."

224
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,000
You:  ""She"?"

225
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Mirari:  "A-Ah, no! It's nothing!"

226
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Mirari:  "I-I was just talking to myself, that's all! Haha... ha..."

227
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:12,000
*Clearly hoping to avoid questioning, Mirari quickly brings the fork to her mouth and takes another bite.*

228
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:18,000
*The moment she does, her lips curl up at the sides, and a joyful smile appears on her face.*

229
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:23,000
*After a few tries, Mirari has gotten the hang of eating with a fork.*

230
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:30,000
*Fueled by hunger, she devours most of the noodles in no time at all, leaving little more than water behind.*

231
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:36,000
*If I'm not careful, she might finish her own portion first and then start on mine.*

232
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:42,000
*Once the two of us have finished eating, I grab our bowls and take them into the kitchen.*

233
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:45,000
Mirari:  "Ah! Are you going to wash those?"

234
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:47,000
You:  "That's the plan."

235
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:52,000
You:  "Unless you'd like to give them both one more lick before I do?"

236
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Mirari:  "{i}Uuu...{/i} Don't remind me of my shameful behavior."

237
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Mirari:  "Hunger truly does turn one into a different person."

238
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:05,000
Mirari:  "B-Be that as it may, I was not going to ask if I could lick the bowls."

239
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:11,000
Mirari:  "Rather than that, uhm... I was just thinking that maybe... if you'd like..."

240
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Mirari:  "...I could clean them for you?"

241
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:17,000
You:  "You... want to clean the dishes?"

242
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,000
*Mirari nods vigorously.*

243
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:25,000
Mirari:  "It's the least I can do after you treated me to such a scrumptious meal."

244
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
You:  "Uhh, okay then."

245
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:34,000
You:  "Look, I'm not going to turn down an offer for help, but... do you even know {i}how{/i} to clean dishes?"

246
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Mirari:  "Of course I do."

247
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Mirari:  "Why wouldn't I know something that simple?"

248
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:46,000
*Mirari tilts her head and gazes at me with an expression of apparent confusion on her face.*

249
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:51,000
You:  "...So forks are new to you, but you know how to wash dishes?"

250
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:54,000
You:  "Fine. If you say you can do it, be my guest."

251
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:57,000
Mirari:  "Y-Yes, I will! Thank you, [player_name]!"

252
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:03,000
*Mirari happily takes my place in front of the sink, which is currently filled with dishes.*

253
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:12,000
*Displaying unexpected knowledge of human appliances, she carefully turns the handle next to the tap, causing water to flood the sink.*

254
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:20,000
*She then twists it back the other way in order to stop the flow of water, and finally takes one of the bowls in hand.*

255
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,000
*(Huh... That's rather surprising.)*

256
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:31,000
*(For someone whose seemed so skittish from the moment she woke up, Mirari seems to be unexpectedly familiar with human inventions.)*

257
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:41,000
*(Maybe half-wolves are more civilized than I thought? I'd always pictured them as wild beasts, who ran around naked and hunted with their claws and teeth.)*

258
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:50,000
*(Despite that, Mirari has been clothed since the moment she showed up here, and she hasn't done anything particularly strange or unruly.)*

259
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:58,000
*(If anything, she's like an ordinary human being who's lived on the brink of society for just a little bit too long.)*

260
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:04,000
*As I compare Mirari to an ordinary human being, my mind flashes back to the moment I found her.*

261
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:10,000
*(Cold, pale, and shivering. Dressed in human clothing. Seeking shelter in a cabin.)*

262
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:15,000
*(Apart from her ears and tail, everything about her screams "human".)*

263
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:20,000
*While thinking back to our initial encounter, one more thought crosses my mind.*

264
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:30,000
*Having found her dressed in wet, disheveled clothing, I made sure to remove Mirari's clothes, then wash and dry them before dressing her once more.*

265
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:36,000
*At that time, even though it was not my intention, I did get a good look at her naked body.*

266
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,000
*(Yep. Just like a human alright.)*

267
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,000
You:  "......"

268
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:42,000
*(Agh, wait! What am I thinking about!?)*

269
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:46,000
*(Bad [player_name]! Get your mind out of the gutter.)*

270
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:51,000
*Just as I pull myself back to reality, Mirari suddenly turns around to face me.*

271
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,000
Mirari:  "Okay, all done!"

272
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,000
You:  "...Huh?"

273
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:57,000
Mirari:  "The dishes. I've finished cleaning them."

274
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
*I unconsciously turn my head towards the sink.*

275
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:08,000
*To my surprise, the sink, which was filled with plates and utensils I've been meaning to clean for days now, is empty.*

276
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:14,000
*All of the items which needed washing have been cleaned and placed on the rack to dry.*

277
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:17,000
You:  "You... cleaned {i}everything{/i}?"

278
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:23,000
Mirari:  "Of course! I couldn't just clean one or two bowls and call it a day's work."

279
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:27,000
You:  "Well... I wouldn't have blamed you if you had."

280
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:30,000
You:  "Really, you didn't need to do all of this."

281
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:35,000
Mirari:  "Don't be silly. I did this because I wanted to, not because I had to."

282
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:41,000
Mirari:  "Besides, if I'm going to be staying here, I need to make sure I earn my keep."

283
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,000
You:  "Oh... Okay then."

284
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:46,000
You:  "As long as you're fine with it, I guess."

285
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:52,000
*Shuffling off with a bright smile on her face, Mirari quickly disappears into the next room.*

286
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:58,000
*The moment she does, her words dawn on me, and a look of confusion creeps onto my face.*

287
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:01,000
*(...Wait. "Staying here"? "Earn my keep"?)*

288
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:06,000
*(Mirari was just talking about the night she's already stayed... right?)*

289
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:10,000
*(Or is she actually assuming that I'll let her stay another?)*

290
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:14,000
*I look out the window as I contemplate kicking Mirari out.*

291
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:21,000
*No matter how nice Mirari is, it's against the rules for humans to associate with half-humans in any way.*

292
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:22,000
You:  "Mmm..."

293
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:27,000
You:  "Even though the snowstorm has died down, it may not be over yet."

294
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:37,000
You:  "And even if it {i}is{/i} over, the snow underfoot is likely to have been dislodged and moved around by the storm, making it dangerous to walk on."

295
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:47,000
You:  "If one adds to that the blistering cold, not to mention Mirari's near-death experience, it's clear that sending her out would not be a good idea."

296
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:51,000
*({i}sigh...{/i} I can't kick her out. Not yet, at least.)*

297
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:59,000
*(No matter how much I prefer to be alone, I'd be eaten away by guilt if I sent that nice young girl to her death.)*

298
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:09,000
*(Besides, it's not like I can't accommodate one more person for a night or two. And I {i}am{/i} curious about how half-humans like Mirari live...)*

299
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:18,000
*(For now, let's just call this a sleepover. And then in a couple of days, when Mirari is feeling better, we'll go our separate ways.)*

300
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:24,000
Mirari:  "Okay! I've finished dusting, tidying up the storeroom, and washing your clothes."

301
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:28,000
Mirari:  "Please tell me what you would like me to do next."

302
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:34,000
*I stare at Mirari in blank amazement as she announces her productivity with vigor.*

303
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:46,000
*A short while ago, when Mirari asked if there was anything else she could do to help out, I half-heartedly listed several chores which I had been putting off doing myself.*

304
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:54,000
*To my surprise, Mirari seems to have completed all of the tasks I offered to her - far more quickly than I would have.*

305
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:56,000
You:  "You're done already?"

306
00:23:56,000 --> 00:24:00,000
You:  "Seriously!? I've been trying to get those out for months!"

307
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:03,000
You:  "How are you so good at this, Mirari?"

308
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:09,000
You:  "I don't think I've ever known a human being half as prompt or hard-working as you are."

309
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:12,000
Mirari:  "Ehehe... Y-You're praising me too much."

310
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:15,000
Mirari:  "I'm really not anything special."

311
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:18,000
You:  "Don't sell yourself short, Mirari."

312
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:25,000
You:  "Not many people could walk straight into the home of another race and outdo them like this."

313
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:31,000
Mirari:  "That's only because I'm used to this kind of work. This is really nothing new to me."

314
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:34,000
*I raise an eyebrow at Mirari's odd response.*

315
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:36,000
*{i}*bang* *bang* *bang*{/i}*

316
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:38,000
Fuyu:  "{size=+6}Princess!!{/size}"

317
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:45,000
*Mirari freezes as she hears someone shout, seemingly frightened by the voice of the one calling out.*

318
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:51,000
*Rather than pay her reaction any mind, however, I turn towards the door in irritation.*

319
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:53,000
You:  "Oh, come {i}on!{/i}"

320
00:24:53,000 --> 00:25:02,000
You:  "I chose this place because it's supposed to be {i}away{/i} from civilization. How have I gotten two visitors in as many days?"

321
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:07,000
You:  "When I get my hands on the agent who sold me this place, I'll--"

322
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:08,000
Fuyu:  "Princess!!"

323
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:09,000
You:  "Uwah!!?"

324
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:13,000
*The moment I open the door, my body is thrown to the floor.*

325
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:18,000
*I'm barreled over in a heartbeat, before I can even lay eyes on the interloper.*

326
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:19,000
You:  "...Wolf-girl?"

327
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:25,000
*My eyes widen in amazement as I spot yet another girl with furry ears and a tail.*

328
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:32,000
*I slowly raise to my feet, taking my eyes off her only for a second as I close and lock the door once more.*

329
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:35,000
You:  "Mirari, is this girl a friend of--"

330
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:36,000
Fuyu:  "Princess!"

331
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:37,000
Mirari:  "Eep!"

332
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:41,000
*Mirari cowers behind the couch as the new girl shouts at her.*

333
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:44,000
*(Hmm, maybe they aren't friends after all.)*

334
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:46,000
*(...Wait a minute. "Princess"?)*

335
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:53,000
*Curious about the girls' relationship, I decide to butt out for a minute and allow them to converse.*

336
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:56,000
Mirari:  "Why... Why did you follow me here?"

337
00:25:56,000 --> 00:26:00,000
Mirari:  "I should have made my intentions perfectly clear."

338
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:02,000
Fuyu:  "Don't ask stupid questions!"

339
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:07,000
Fuyu:  "You're our princess! Of course someone is going to come looking for you."

340
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:12,000
Mirari:  "B-But... it was a blizzard out there! You could have been killed!"

341
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:15,000
Fuyu:  "The same goes for you, princess."

342
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Fuyu:  "How could I not be worried when you suddenly went out in the middle of that storm!?"

343
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:24,000
Mirari:  "I... I didn't ask you to worry about me."

344
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:27,000
Mirari:  "I can take care of myself, you know."

345
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:34,000
Fuyu:  "Oh yeah. I can totally see that by the fact that you're seeking refuge with a {i}human{/i}."

346
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:39,000
Fuyu:  "How unsightly... Our princess, boarding with some low-life human."

347
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:42,000
Mirari:  "[player_name] is not a low-life!"

348
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Fuyu:  "And none of that would have been necessary if you'd just stayed with the pack!"

349
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:55,000
Fuyu:  "You can't just suddenly declare that you're leaving, princess. It doesn't work like that."

350
00:26:55,000 --> 00:26:57,000
Mirari:  "I... I know that..."

351
00:26:57,000 --> 00:27:02,000
Mirari:  "I know I shouldn't have left without giving notice like that... but--"

352
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:03,000
Fuyu:  "But nothing."

353
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:07,000
Fuyu:  "You are safe now, and that's all that matters."

354
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:14,000
Fuyu:  "Now come. Let us return and tell your mother the good news. She must be worried sick about you."

355
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:15,000
Mirari:  "......"

356
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:16,000
Fuyu:  "...Princess?"

357
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:18,000
Mirari:  "I... don't want to go."

358
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:19,000
Fuyu:  "What!?"

359
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:23,000
Fuyu:  "What do you mean you don't want to go back!?"

360
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:28,000
Fuyu:  "This is our pack we're talking about! You {i}must{/i} return!"

361
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:29,000
Mirari:  "......"

362
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:31,000
Mirari:  "I'm not going."

363
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:33,000
Fuyu:  "The hell you aren't!"

364
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:39,000
*The aggressive half-wolf grabs Mirari by the wrist and forcefully drags her towards the door.*

365
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:45,000
*Mirari tries to resist, but it's clear that this new girl is much stronger than she is.*

366
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:46,000
Fuyu:  "{i}Uuu...{/i}"

367
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:54,000
You:  "Listen to me. Just last night, Mirari was both freezing and starving. She could have died, given the state she was in."

368
00:27:54,000 --> 00:28:00,000
You:  "I'm not about to let you drag her out into the cold to her death. Do you understand?"

369
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:01,000
Fuyu:  "...Mm."

370
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:03,000
*Sulking, the girl nods.*

371
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:10,000
*Faced with the very real prospect of Mirari's death, she can't bring herself to refute my words.*

372
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:16,000
Mirari:  "[player_name], does this mean... you'll let me stay a little while longer?"

373
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:22,000
You:  "That's right. Just until you're healthy enough to be up and about on your own."

374
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:24,000
Mirari:  "Oh, thank goodness."

375
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:30,000
Mirari:  "Thank you so much, [player_name]. You have no idea how much this means to me."

376
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:33,000
Fuyu:  "It's nothing worth being thankful over."

377
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Mirari:  "Now, now. Don't be like that, Fuyu."

378
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:40,000
Mirari:  "Oh, I know! Why don't I make lunch for the three of us?"

379
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:41,000
Fuyu:  "Lunch!?"

380
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:43,000
You:  "{i}Three{/i} of us?"

381
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:46,000
*I raise an eyebrow at Mirari's proposition.*

382
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:52,000
*Fuyu, on the other hand, begins to wag her tail, with her ears clearly pricked up.*

383
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:58,000
Mirari:  "That's right! Won't it be wonderful to eat hot food together in this warm, cozy cabin?"

384
00:28:58,000 --> 00:29:04,000
Fuyu:  "W-Well... When you put it that way, I guess it doesn't sound {i}that{/i} bad."

385
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:07,000
You:  "I never said that this rude girl could stay."

386
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:11,000
*Upon hearing my complaint, Mirari's ears begin to droop.*

387
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:18,000
*She looks up at me with big, watery eyes, as though silently pleading for her friend to join us.*

388
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:21,000
You:  "I-I mean it! No uninvited guests!"

389
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:26,000
You:  "A... And besides, we just ate breakfast. It's too soon to be--"

390
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:28,000
Fuyu:  "{i}*whimper*{/i}"

391
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:32,000
*Fuyu stands beside Mirari and pulls the exact same maneuver.*

392
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:38,000
*Like a pair of puppies, they look up at me pleadingly, appealing to my conscience and humanity.*

393
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:40,000
You:  "Fine. Do as you please."

394
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Mirari:  "Yes!"

395
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:42,000
Fuyu:  "Woohoo!"

396
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:47,000
*The moment I give my consent, Mirari and Fuyu both start to jump up and down.*

397
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:54,000
*Tails wagging, teeth showing, they both appear to be thrilled by the notion of sharing a hot meal together.*

398
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:57,000
Mirari:  "This calls for a celebration!"

399
00:29:57,000 --> 00:30:03,000
Mirari:  "I'll make something extra special, with plenty to go around for all three of us!"

400
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:05,000
You:  "Uhh... No. Don't do that."

401
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:10,000
You:  "Like I said, we only just ate breakfast, so I'm really not hungry."

402
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:13,000
Fuyu:  "Something special? Like what?"

403
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:19,000
Mirari:  "I've only tried one dish so far, but I'm sure the others are just as delicious."

404
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:22,000
You:  "Hey, are you two even listening to me?"

405
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:26,000
You:  "No celebrating, and no serving for me. Got that?"

406
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:28,000
Fuyu:  "Ooh, I can't wait!"

407
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:34,000
Fuyu:  "I'm getting hungry just thinking about eating the princess's delicious cooking!"

408
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:37,000
Mirari:  "Heehee... I'm glad to hear it."

409
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:44,000
Mirari:  "I'll get started right away. Let me just head to the storeroom to find something to cook with."

410
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:52,000
*Ignoring me until the very end, the two girls run off towards the storeroom, enthralled by the promise of delicious food.*

411
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:57,000
You:  "{i}sigh...{/i} Forget it. They'll be gone soon enough anyway."

412
00:30:57,000 --> 00:31:02,000
You:  "For now, let's see if Mirari is as good at cooking as she is at cleaning."

413
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:05,000
Fuyu:  "{i}*munch* *munch* *munch*{/i}"

414
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:08,000
Fuyu:  "Mmmm! So good! {i}*slurp*{/i}"

415
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:13,000
Fuyu:  "Princess, you have outdone yourself! {i}*munch* *munch* *munch*{/i}"

416
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:17,000
*I watch on with both caution and amazement as Fuyu eats her fill.*

417
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:27,000
*Given a bowl full of canned peas and other kept foods, all either steamed or stewed to perfection by Mirari, Fuyu hasn't put her bowl down once.*

418
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:33,000
*(I want to tell her to use cutlery... but at this point, I'm afraid to interrupt.)*

419
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:40,000
*From the beginning, Fuyu has been either lowering her face to the bowl, or lifting the bowl to her face.*

420
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:45,000
*The fact that Mirari brought out spoons has apparently failed to register.*

421
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:48,000
*(I suppose I shouldn't be surprised.)*

422
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:55,000
*(This girl was subjected to the same terrain and conditions as Mirari. It makes sense that she'd be famished.)*

423
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:58,000
*(Maybe I should offer her my bowl as well?)*

424
00:31:58,000 --> 00:32:01,000
*The moment I place a hand on my bowl--*

425
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:05,000
Mirari:  "Ah, [player_name]! You're going to eat as well?"

426
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:07,000
You:  "Huh? Oh, no. I was just--"

427
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:14,000
Mirari:  "It's okay. They're all foods from your storeroom, so this should definitely suit a human palate."

428
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:17,000
You:  "That's... really not what's holding me back."

429
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:20,000
Mirari:  "It's really good, I promise."

430
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:29,000
Mirari:  "I'm actually quite pleased with how this meal turned out, and I would love for you to try it and give me your feedback."

431
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:31,000
You:  "{i}haa...{/i} I don't know..."

432
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:37,000
Mirari:  "Look, I'll make it easy for you. You don't even have to raise your hand."

433
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:39,000
Mirari:  "Just say "ahhhhn"!"

434
00:32:39,000 --> 00:32:46,000
*Mirari uses her spoon, the one she's been eating with until now, to scoop up some of the food in my bowl.*

435
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:50,000
You:  "I-It's fine, really! Like I said before, I'm not hungry."

436
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:51,000
Mirari:  "......"

437
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:52,000
Mirari:  ""Ahhhhn"!"

438
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:54,000
You:  "No, I just said--"

439
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:55,000
Mirari:  ""Ahhhhn"!"

440
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:56,000
You:  "......"

441
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:57,000
You:  "A-Ahhhh..."

442
00:32:57,000 --> 00:33:00,000
*Sighing internally, I finally give in.*

443
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:08,000
*The moment I do, Mirari happily places her spoon in my mouth, at which point I close my lips and trap the spoon's contents.*

444
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:14,000
*I chew the soft, warm mush, which doesn't really need to be chewed at all, and then swallow.*

445
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:16,000
Mirari:  "H-How was it?"

446
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:18,000
Mirari:  "Did you... like it?"

447
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:19,000
Mirari:  "......"

448
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:23,000
*Mirari turns away as Fuyu casually reveals her situation.*

449
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:25,000
You:  "Woah, hold on a second."

450
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:31,000
You:  "Mirari, you were taught to cook so that you could please your "future mate"?"

451
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:35,000
Fuyu:  "That's right! It's Mirari's responsibility to--"

452
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:36,000
Fuyu:  "Mm-mmph!"

453
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:41,000
*Mirari hurriedly covers Fuyu's mouth before she can say anything else.*

454
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Mirari:  "A-Ahahaha, what manner of nonsense are you spouting, Fuyu?"

455
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:51,000
Mirari:  "I cook because I enjoy watching others eat my cooking, that's all!"

456
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:59,000
Mirari:  "{size=-2}...If I planned on mating with the next alpha male, I wouldn't have ran away in the first place.{/size}"

457
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:03,000
*Mirari's words intrigue me, but I decide not to pry.*

458
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:15,000
*Whatever has happened to these two girls until this point is none of my business. And if Mirari would rather run away from home than find a mate, that is completely up to her.*

459
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:24,000
*I'm just a kind stranger who took pity on a near-death young girl. What she does with the life I saved is not for me to decide.*

460
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:25,000
Mirari:  "Mmmm..."

461
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:26,000
Fuyu:  "Fuuu..."

462
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:27,000
You:  "...Seriously?"

463
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:32,000
You:  "Don't you think you should at least wait for the food to settle first?"

464
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:34,000
Fuyu:  "Mmm... So full..."

465
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:37,000
Mirari:  "[player_name], you should eat more too..."

466
00:34:37,000 --> 00:34:40,000
You:  "I already ate plenty, thank you."

467
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:44,000
You:  "Though it was nothing compared to what the two of you ate."

468
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:53,000
*Shortly after the three of us finish eating, Mirari and Fuyu both let out big yawns, then curl up next to one another on the couch.*

469
00:34:53,000 --> 00:35:04,000
*Sharing their body warmth, as I imagine they would often do out in the snow, the two girls snuggle up close to one another with looks of contentment on their faces.*

470
00:35:04,000 --> 00:35:12,000
*(Sheesh. I want to tell them off for going to sleep right after eating, but... when I look at them both like this...)*

471
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:15,000
*Without realizing it, I begin to smile.*

472
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:21,000
*Just yesterday, I found Mirari on the floor, cold and shivering as she narrowly avoided death.*

473
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:31,000
*Then today, Fuyu suddenly barged into my cabin. She's been running her mouth all day, and we haven't enjoyed a moment of silence since she arrived.*

474
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:36,000
*But for now, if only temporarily, the two girls seem to be at peace.*

475
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:47,000
*Sleeping soundly, comforted by the presence of their partner, the two wolf-girls look like a pair of young pups, clinging to one another in an unfamiliar environment.*

476
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:55,000
*Previously afraid for the other's safety, they have now found one another once more, and can finally be at ease.*

477
00:35:55,000 --> 00:36:00,000
*({i}sigh...{/i} I suppose I can let Fuyu stay for tonight as well.)*

478
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:04,000
*(I'd feel bad, trying to separate the two of them now.)*

479
00:36:04,000 --> 00:36:12,000
*(Besides... I've been alone out here for a long time now. A day or two in the company of these girls shouldn't kill me.)*

480
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:16,000
*I enter my bedroom for a moment and open the closet.*

481
00:36:16,000 --> 00:36:22,000
*A few seconds later, I return with a blanket in my arms, which I then use to cover the girls.*

482
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:28,000
You:  "Even if you leave this cabin tomorrow, for tonight, you two are my guests, so..."

483
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:29,000
You:  "...Sleep well."

484
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:37,000
*Resisting the urge to ruffle the girls' hair as they sleep, I return to the kitchen with our bowls and utensils to clean up.*

485
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:42,000
*For now, I'll let the girls rest. And tomorrow... we'll see what awaits us.*

486
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:46,000
*I wake up bright and early as the morning sun lights up my room.*

487
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:57,000
*In spite of the hellish blizzard from two days ago, it seems that the weather has begun to clear up, and the freezing cold is becoming more tolerable by the day.*

488
00:36:57,000 --> 00:37:02,000
*At this rate, I'll soon be able to go outside without over-dressing.*

489
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:08,000
*Filled with optimistic thoughts, I leave my bedroom and return to the main living area.*

490
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:16,000
*The moment I enter the room, a strong odor reaches my nose, and I instinctively turn to look towards the kitchen.*

491
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:17,000
Fuyu:  "Come onnnn~"

492
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:19,000
Fuyu:  "Isn't it done yeeetttt~?"

493
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:25,000
Mirari:  "No matter how many times you ask, breakfast isn't going to be ready any quicker."

494
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:31,000
Mirari:  "If you're looking for something to do, why don't you go wake up [player_name]?"

495
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:32,000
Fuyu:  "Funyah!!?"

496
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:37,000
*Fuyu jumps back in surprise as she suddenly hears my voice directly behind her.*

497
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:40,000
Mirari:  "Oh, [player_name]! You're awake."

498
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:44,000
Mirari:  "You're just in time. Breakfast will be ready shortly."

499
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:49,000
Mirari:  "Please, take a seat. I'll bring the food out when it's ready."

500
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:50,000
You:  "Oh... Okay."

501
00:37:50,000 --> 00:37:52,000
You:  "I'll leave it to you then."

502
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:59,000
*Having no intention of stopping Mirari while she's cooking, I do as she suggests and sit down on the couch.*

503
00:37:59,000 --> 00:38:00,000
Fuyu:  "Grrr..."

504
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:04,000
Fuyu:  "Miserable human, preying on the princess's kind nature...!"

505
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:09,000
You:  "Oh, shut up. It's not like I asked her to cook me breakfast or anything."

506
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:15,000
You:  "Besides, you seemed pretty eager to take advantage of her kindness yourself."

507
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:23,000
You:  "Just a second ago you were sitting on the floor with your tail wagging, like a dog waiting for its master to feed it."

508
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:24,000
Fuyu:  "A... A dog!?"

509
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:27,000
Fuyu:  "You're comparing me to a dog!?"

510
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:31,000
You:  "Well, yeah. That {i}is{/i} what you looked like."

511
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:36,000
You:  "Besides, dogs and wolves are pretty much the same anyway, right?"

512
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:38,000
Fuyu:  "D-D-Do not insult me, human!"

513
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:41,000
Fuyu:  "Wolves are nothing like dogs!"

514
00:38:41,000 --> 00:38:44,000
*I smirk to myself as I enjoy Fuyu's reactions.*

515
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:45,000
You:  "Oh? How so?"

516
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:50,000
You:  "I thought dogs and wolves were descendants of the same ancestors?"

517
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:56,000
Fuyu:  "That doesn't mean we're the same! You wouldn't mix up a human and a monkey, would you?"

518
00:38:56,000 --> 00:39:02,000
Fuyu:  "Dogs are pitiful, subservient creatures who only know how to bow before human beings."

519
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:09,000
Fuyu:  "Wolves, on the other hand, are proud hunters, who don't need the help of any other race to survive!"

520
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:11,000
You:  "Uh-huh, uh-huh."

521
00:39:11,000 --> 00:39:21,000
You:  "So a proud, independent creature like a wolf would {i}never{/i} do something like... I don't know... sleep in a human's cabin and eat their food?"

522
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:22,000
Fuyu:  "Urk!"

523
00:39:22,000 --> 00:39:25,000
*Fuyu's face contorts in displeasure.*

524
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:31,000
*Her claims of independence hold little weight at the moment, given our current predicament.*

525
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:34,000
Fuyu:  "{i}Uuu...{/i} That's... That's different..."

526
00:39:34,000 --> 00:39:35,000
You:  "Is it?"

527
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:36,000
Fuyu:  "Grrr..."

528
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:38,000
Fuyu:  "W-Well, what about you!?"

529
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:39,000
You:  "Me?"

530
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:43,000
Fuyu:  "Yeah! What are you even {i}doing{/i} out here?"

531
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:48,000
Fuyu:  "What, were you exiled or something? Is this your punishment?"

532
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:54,000
Fuyu:  "Were... Were you caught doing something heinous, and banished from society forever?"

533
00:39:54,000 --> 00:40:03,000
Fuyu:  "Yeah... That must be it. You did something unforgivable, and you were sent out here to live the rest of your days in solitude."

534
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:10,000
Fuyu:  "How could I have missed this before? Now I feel endangered just being in the same room as you."

535
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:15,000
*A look of panic spreads across Fuyu's face as she slowly backs away from me.*

536
00:40:15,000 --> 00:40:18,000
You:  "Would you please stop smearing my good name?"

537
00:40:18,000 --> 00:40:25,000
You:  "I moved out here of my own free will because I don't get along well with other people. That's it."

538
00:40:25,000 --> 00:40:32,000
*Hearing my explanation, Fuyu stops backing away and begins to look at me with eyes filled with curiosity.*

539
00:40:32,000 --> 00:40:35,000
Fuyu:  "You... don't like other humans?"

540
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:38,000
You:  "That's the short version, yeah."

541
00:40:38,000 --> 00:40:40,000
Fuyu:  "Then... what about us?"

542
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:42,000
You:  "...You and Mirari?"

543
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:43,000
*Fuyu nods.*

544
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:46,000
Fuyu:  "You let us both into your home--"

545
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:49,000
You:  "You {i}forced your way{/i} into my home."

546
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:53,000
Fuyu:  "...And you haven't tried to kick us out or anything."

547
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:57,000
You:  "Given another few days, I might think quite differently."

548
00:40:57,000 --> 00:40:59,000
Fuyu:  "Hmm... Is that so...?"

549
00:40:59,000 --> 00:41:01,000
*Fuyu analyzes my answer carefully.*

550
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:07,000
*She doesn't appear to be particularly invested in my answer, nor does it bring her any joy.*

551
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:12,000
*Her question was one posed out of curiosity, with no ulterior motive.*

552
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:16,000
Fuyu:  "Well, I wouldn't worry about you changing your mind."

553
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:23,000
Fuyu:  "After all, the princess and I won't be staying long enough for you to get sick of our company."

554
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:29,000
Fuyu:  "No matter how warm is it here, we must return to our pack as soon as possible."

555
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:30,000
*(That works for me.)*

556
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:38,000
*(A couple of nights is more than enough. I've done my good deed for the year; now I just want to be left alone.)*

557
00:41:38,000 --> 00:41:41,000
*I nod in agreement with Fuyu's statement.*

558
00:41:41,000 --> 00:41:46,000
You:  "I understand. I won't try to stop you from returning to your pack."

559
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:51,000
You:  "As soon as the two of you are ready to leave, I'll see you off."

560
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:54,000
Fuyu:  "Okay, princess. It's time to go."

561
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:56,000
Mirari:  "F... Fuyu...?"

562
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:59,000
Mirari:  "What are you talking about?"

563
00:41:59,000 --> 00:42:05,000
Fuyu:  "Please don't play dumb, princess. You know exactly what I'm talking about."

564
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:10,000
Fuyu:  "You've had your fun. Now it's time that we returned to our pack."

565
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:11,000
Mirari:  "...Already?"

566
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:13,000
Mirari:  "But... we only just..."

567
00:42:13,000 --> 00:42:19,000
Fuyu:  "That's my point. We must leave now, before we grow accustomed to this lifestyle."

568
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:24,000
Fuyu:  "Relying on humans is no good, princess. We must return to our own kind."

569
00:42:24,000 --> 00:42:31,000
*Once the three of us have finished eating breakfast, Fuyu wastes no time before making good on her promise.*

570
00:42:31,000 --> 00:42:40,000
*The satisfied smile indicative of a full belly disappears from her face, replaced by a serious expression, and a tone of voice to match.*

571
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:43,000
Mirari:  "Do we... have to go back, no matter what?"

572
00:42:43,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Mirari:  "I quite like it here, and--"

573
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:47,000
Fuyu:  "Princess."

574
00:42:47,000 --> 00:42:49,000
*Fuyu grabs Mirari by the shoulder.*

575
00:42:49,000 --> 00:42:51,000
Fuyu:  "Do not be selfish."

576
00:42:51,000 --> 00:42:53,000
Fuyu:  "It is time for us to return."

577
00:42:53,000 --> 00:42:54,000
Mirari:  "But I..."

578
00:42:54,000 --> 00:42:58,000
*Mirari turns away from Fuyu and casts me a sidelong glance.*

579
00:42:58,000 --> 00:43:03,000
Mirari:  "I-It's okay if I stay here awhile longer, isn't it, [player_name]?"

580
00:43:03,000 --> 00:43:04,000
Fuyu:  "Princess--"

581
00:43:04,000 --> 00:43:09,000
Mirari:  "I won't cause any trouble, or do anything you tell me not to."

582
00:43:09,000 --> 00:43:13,000
Mirari:  "I'll cook and clean, and I'll help out as much as I can!"

583
00:43:13,000 --> 00:43:15,000
Mirari:  "So... please..."

584
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:17,000
Fuyu:  "...Princess..."

585
00:43:17,000 --> 00:43:20,000
*I avert my gaze as Mirari begins to plead.*

586
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:25,000
*No matter the reason for her desperation, I can't afford to let her stay.*

587
00:43:25,000 --> 00:43:35,000
*My supplies were really only enough to last me through winter, and there's also the ethical question of my interfering in half-human affairs.*

588
00:43:35,000 --> 00:43:40,000
*Plus Fuyu said it herself: Mirari's family and friends are waiting for her.*

589
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:43,000
*Her place is with them, not here with me.*

590
00:43:43,000 --> 00:43:44,000
You:  "Mirari..."

591
00:43:44,000 --> 00:43:47,000
Mirari:  "Please, [player_name]! Just let me--"

592
00:43:47,000 --> 00:43:50,000
*I place my index finger on Mirari's soft lips.*

593
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:55,000
You:  "Mirari, don't you think you've worried your family enough as it is?"

594
00:43:55,000 --> 00:43:58,000
You:  "You belong with the rest of your pack."

595
00:43:58,000 --> 00:43:59,000
Mirari:  "......"

596
00:43:59,000 --> 00:44:01,000
Mirari:  "I... I understand..."

597
00:44:01,000 --> 00:44:05,000
*Mirari gives up without a fight as I quickly shut her down.*

598
00:44:05,000 --> 00:44:11,000
*Her eyes downcast, she slowly trudges towards the door, not looking back even once.*

599
00:44:11,000 --> 00:44:15,000
Fuyu:  "...Thank you for not making this difficult, [player_name]."

600
00:44:15,000 --> 00:44:23,000
Fuyu:  "Mirari may act defiant at times, but she's a reasonable person. Hearing you tell her to go home should be enough."

601
00:44:23,000 --> 00:44:25,000
You:  "Yeah... No problem."

602
00:44:25,000 --> 00:44:30,000
*Feeling bad about turning Mirari down, I find it hard to look Fuyu in the eye.*

603
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:34,000
*As my eyes wander around the cabin, I suddenly realize something.*

604
00:44:34,000 --> 00:44:36,000
You:  "Oh, hold on a second."

605
00:44:36,000 --> 00:44:37,000
Fuyu:  "Mmm?"

606
00:44:37,000 --> 00:44:42,000
*I take a pair of coats off the coat-rack and present them to Fuyu.*

607
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:44,000
You:  "Here, take these."

608
00:44:44,000 --> 00:44:47,000
*In response to my offer, Fuyu shakes her head.*

609
00:44:47,000 --> 00:44:51,000
Fuyu:  "I appreciate your kindness, but I'll have to decline."

610
00:44:51,000 --> 00:44:56,000
Fuyu:  "Our tolerance for the cold is significantly greater than that of humans."

611
00:44:56,000 --> 00:45:02,000
Fuyu:  "In anything less than a blizzard, garments such as those will only get in our way."

612
00:45:02,000 --> 00:45:03,000
You:  "Oh... I see."

613
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:07,000
*I take another look at the outfits Mirari and Fuyu are wearing.*

614
00:45:07,000 --> 00:45:15,000
*If those two are comfortable while wearing so little, they must indeed have a far greater tolerance for the cold than I do.*

615
00:45:15,000 --> 00:45:18,000
You:  "In that case, I guess this is goodbye."

616
00:45:18,000 --> 00:45:21,000
You:  "Maybe I'll see you two again some day?"

617
00:45:21,000 --> 00:45:23,000
Fuyu:  "Don't count on it."

618
00:45:23,000 --> 00:45:31,000
Fuyu:  "We live on the other side of this mountain. Were it not for the snowstorm, we would have never met to begin with."

619
00:45:31,000 --> 00:45:34,000
Fuyu:  "This shall be our final farewell."

620
00:45:34,000 --> 00:45:39,000
*Confidently asserting so, Fuyu turns her back on me and heads towards the door.*

621
00:45:39,000 --> 00:45:41,000
*As she does so, however--*

622
00:45:41,000 --> 00:45:42,000
Mirari:  "......"

623
00:45:42,000 --> 00:45:45,000
*Mirari no longer seems ready to leave.*

624
00:45:45,000 --> 00:45:46,000
You:  "Mirari...?"

625
00:45:46,000 --> 00:45:48,000
*Mirari's eyes shift back and forth.*

626
00:45:48,000 --> 00:45:54,000
*It seems like she wants to say something to me, but can't quite bring herself to speak.*

627
00:45:54,000 --> 00:45:56,000
Fuyu:  "Come along, princess."

628
00:45:56,000 --> 00:45:59,000
Fuyu:  "Let us not delay our departure any further."

629
00:45:59,000 --> 00:46:04,000
*At Fuyu's command, Mirari lowers her head and walks along obediently.*

630
00:46:04,000 --> 00:46:11,000
*Mirari slowly unlocks the door, then regretfully sets foot outside, gently pushed along by her dear friend.*

631
00:46:11,000 --> 00:46:14,000
*Moments later, the door slams shut, and at last...*

632
00:46:14,000 --> 00:46:16,000
*I am all alone once more.*

633
00:46:16,000 --> 00:46:21,000
*For the next hour or so, I find myself wandering around the cabin aimlessly.*

634
00:46:21,000 --> 00:46:27,000
*Having already slept and eaten, there's honestly very little remaining that I need to do.*

635
00:46:27,000 --> 00:46:38,000
*I have enough supplies to last for a while yet, it's too cold outside to think about working, and my hobbies are all the type to be enjoyed while resting idly.*

636
00:46:38,000 --> 00:46:40,000
*Put simply, I'm bored.*

637
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:45,000
*(Solitude may be its own reward, but the cost at which it comes is clear.)*

638
00:46:45,000 --> 00:46:55,000
*(There's nothing to do out here during the colder months. And even when things warm up, the choices can't compare to those available in the city.)*

639
00:46:55,000 --> 00:47:05,000
*(At least with those two wolf-girls around, things were a bit more lively. Other people are a nuisance, but a pet could be just what I need.)*

640
00:47:05,000 --> 00:47:11,000
*(That being said... what kind of pet would be suitable out in the middle of nowhere like this?)*

641
00:47:11,000 --> 00:47:17,000
*Giving myself something to think about, I decide to turn on the radio in the kitchen.*

642
00:47:17,000 --> 00:47:27,000
*After adjusting the frequency and waiting for a short while, I am able to receive the weather forecast, which paints a rather placid picture.*

643
00:47:27,000 --> 00:47:32,000
*(Hmm. Maybe I should go out and get some water while it's still mild outside.)*

644
00:47:32,000 --> 00:47:38,000
*(The weather can change out here at the drop of a hat, so it never hurts to have a surplus.)*

645
00:47:38,000 --> 00:47:44,000
*I grab my coat and head for the door, resolving myself to be slightly more active than usual.*

646
00:47:44,000 --> 00:47:52,000
*Before this pleasant weather changes for the worst, I'm going to sure up my supplies, just as any prudent survivor should.*

647
00:47:52,000 --> 00:47:57,000
You:  "Brr! Who the hell thought it would be a good idea to fetch water?"

648
00:47:57,000 --> 00:48:04,000
You:  "Everything has turned to sludge out there! The entire landscape has changed since before the snowstorm."

649
00:48:04,000 --> 00:48:09,000
*I hurriedly close the door behind me as I return from gathering water.*

650
00:48:09,000 --> 00:48:18,000
*Unfortunately, my trip proves fairly fruitless, as the spring from which I usually gather drinking water has been temporarily blocked off.*

651
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:26,000
*The snowstorm has shifted the terrain, making my usual routes either inaccessible, or far more dangerous than usual.*

652
00:48:26,000 --> 00:48:29,000
You:  "Screw it. I'll just stay inside after all."

653
00:48:29,000 --> 00:48:34,000
You:  "It may be boring to stay indoors all day, but at least it's safe."

654
00:48:34,000 --> 00:48:40,000
*Still shivering slightly, I regretfully remove my coat and flop down on the couch.*

655
00:48:40,000 --> 00:48:50,000
*Covering myself with a blanket, the same one I used to cover the two sleeping wolf-girls yesterday, I settle myself in and try to make myself comfortable.*

656
00:48:50,000 --> 00:48:53,000
You:  "Let's see now... Where did I put the remote?"

657
00:48:53,000 --> 00:48:58,000
You:  "If it isn't within arm's reach, I'm not getting up to look for it."

658
00:48:58,000 --> 00:49:01,000
*I look around the immediate vicinity of the couch.*

659
00:49:01,000 --> 00:49:10,000
*Unfortunately, the remote is nowhere to be seen. It's probably still in the kitchen, from when I last watched TV while cooking.*

660
00:49:10,000 --> 00:49:14,000
You:  "{i}sigh...{/i} I guess I'll just sit here then."

661
00:49:14,000 --> 00:49:16,000
You:  "What a fun person I am."

662
00:49:16,000 --> 00:49:17,000
You:  "...Hmm?"

663
00:49:17,000 --> 00:49:20,000
*As I sit in silence, I notice a faint sound.*

664
00:49:20,000 --> 00:49:26,000
*It sounds like a voice, but it's too quiet for me to understand what they're saying.*

665
00:49:26,000 --> 00:49:29,000
You:  "Oh, great. Now I'm hearing things."

666
00:49:29,000 --> 00:49:33,000
You:  "Maybe I've lived alone out here for too long after all."

667
00:49:33,000 --> 00:49:37,000
*I try to ignore the voice by focusing my mind elsewhere.*

668
00:49:37,000 --> 00:49:45,000
*However, the voice doesn't disappear. It seems to cut in and out, with ample static cropping up in between words.*

669
00:49:45,000 --> 00:49:47,000
You:  "What the heck could that--"

670
00:49:47,000 --> 00:49:49,000
You:  "Oh, right! The radio!"

671
00:49:49,000 --> 00:49:56,000
*I unintentionally rise to my feet and turn towards the kitchen, where I've left the radio turned on.*

672
00:49:56,000 --> 00:50:02,000
*Seeing as how it's battery powered, I figure I'd better turn it off if I'm not using it.*

673
00:50:02,000 --> 00:50:08,000
*Before I can do so, however, I hear something ominous from the other end of the radio.*

674
00:50:08,000 --> 00:50:12,000
Radio:  "...Bad weather... incoming... {i}*screech*{/i}"

675
00:50:12,000 --> 00:50:17,000
Radio:  "...avalanche last night... paths have changed... Advising caution..."

676
00:50:17,000 --> 00:50:20,000
You:  "Phew. It was worse than I thought, huh?"

677
00:50:20,000 --> 00:50:23,000
You:  "Now I'm {i}definitely{/i} not going outside."

678
00:50:23,000 --> 00:50:29,000
*I turn the radio off and grab the TV remote, which is sitting on the kitchen counter.*

679
00:50:29,000 --> 00:50:34,000
*I then return to the living room and sit down on the couch, remote in hand.*

680
00:50:34,000 --> 00:50:37,000
You:  "{i}sigh...{/i} Okay now. Where were we?"

681
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:41,000
You:  "...Ah, yes. Let's find something to watch, shall we?"

682
00:50:41,000 --> 00:50:44,000
You:  "Now, what did I start watching last time?"

683
00:50:44,000 --> 00:50:52,000
*Before I turn on the television, I go to wrap myself in the blanket I had used to cover myself just a moment ago.*

684
00:50:52,000 --> 00:50:57,000
*The second I go to do so, however, I feel a chill run down my spine.*

685
00:50:57,000 --> 00:50:59,000
You:  "...Oh shit. The girls..."

686
00:50:59,000 --> 00:51:06,000
You:  "They wouldn't know about the avalanche last night, or the bad weather that's about to hit."

687
00:51:06,000 --> 00:51:12,000
You:  "Ah hell, how can I sit back and relax knowing that those girls might be in danger?"

688
00:51:12,000 --> 00:51:18,000
You:  "I can watch TV any time. For now, I've got a couple of wolf-girls to track down!"

689
00:51:18,000 --> 00:51:25,000
*Covered in several layers, I head out into the frozen wasteland before me in search of the two wolf-girls.*

690
00:51:25,000 --> 00:51:31,000
*Upon starting my drive, I quickly realize that the cold is the least of my worries.*

691
00:51:31,000 --> 00:51:39,000
*As I noted earlier, and the radio confirmed, all of the usual scenery has changed since I last ventured outside.*

692
00:51:39,000 --> 00:51:46,000
*Familiar landmarks are gone, paths have been blocked off, and solid ground has been replaced by sleet.*

693
00:51:46,000 --> 00:51:50,000
*If I'm not careful, I might wind up getting lost or stuck myself.*

694
00:51:50,000 --> 00:51:54,000
You:  "Okay now, where would those two girls have gone?"

695
00:51:54,000 --> 00:51:59,000
You:  "I've never been to the other side of the mountain, but if memory serves..."

696
00:51:59,000 --> 00:52:05,000
*I follow a vague recollection I have of the map I purchased when I first moved out here.*

697
00:52:05,000 --> 00:52:15,000
*The actual pathways have obviously changed since then, but my memory gives me at least a hint as to the direction in which I should be heading.*

698
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:20,000
You:  "Now then, if I remember correctly, it should be this road here."

699
00:52:20,000 --> 00:52:24,000
You:  "...Or at least it {i}was{/i}, back when there was a road."

700
00:52:24,000 --> 00:52:29,000
*I come to a stop as the road I'm following appears to end abruptly.*

701
00:52:29,000 --> 00:52:36,000
*A few hundred feet in front of me, where there would generally be a road, there is a huge pile of snow.*

702
00:52:36,000 --> 00:52:39,000
*From my point of view, it's impossible to bypass.*

703
00:52:39,000 --> 00:52:43,000
You:  "Oh man... I guess the road is blocked after all."

704
00:52:43,000 --> 00:52:48,000
You:  "Maybe there's a path or something that I just can't see from here?"

705
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:50,000
You:  "If I move in a bit closer--"

706
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:55,000
*I force myself to get out of the truck, shivering as the blizzard rages.*

707
00:52:55,000 --> 00:53:00,000
*My legs may be weary, but my stomach is full, and my body is warm.*

708
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:04,000
*If those girls are out here, I'm going to find them.*

709
00:53:04,000 --> 00:53:05,000
You:  "Mirari! Fuyu!"

710
00:53:05,000 --> 00:53:07,000
You:  "Are you two out here!?"

711
00:53:07,000 --> 00:53:08,000
*......*

712
00:53:08,000 --> 00:53:09,000
You:  "Mirari!"

713
00:53:09,000 --> 00:53:10,000
You:  "Fuyu!"

714
00:53:10,000 --> 00:53:11,000
*......*

715
00:53:11,000 --> 00:53:16,000
*I call out the girls' names as I head closer to the obstructed pathway.*

716
00:53:16,000 --> 00:53:20,000
*As I near the wall of snow, a vague figure appears up ahead.*

717
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:25,000
*Squinting, I try to discern the identity of the being in front of me.*

718
00:53:25,000 --> 00:53:26,000
You:  "Mirari? Fuyu?"

719
00:53:26,000 --> 00:53:28,000
Fuyu:  "...[player_name]...!?"

720
00:53:28,000 --> 00:53:29,000
You:  "Fuyu!"

721
00:53:29,000 --> 00:53:34,000
*Hearing Fuyu's surprised exclamation, I rush over to the figure up ahead.*

722
00:53:34,000 --> 00:53:39,000
*Once I get closer, I realize that it's not just Fuyu; Mirari is with her too.*

723
00:53:39,000 --> 00:53:40,000
*However--*

724
00:53:40,000 --> 00:53:43,000
Fuyu:  "[player_name], please help me!"

725
00:53:43,000 --> 00:53:50,000
Fuyu:  "Mirari suddenly collapsed while we were walking, so I carried her myself, but the path is--"

726
00:53:50,000 --> 00:53:55,000
You:  "I know. Most of the paths have changed, or been blocked off."

727
00:53:55,000 --> 00:53:59,000
You:  "You won't be able to get through here. Not today."

728
00:53:59,000 --> 00:54:00,000
Fuyu:  "...Eh?"

729
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:02,000
Fuyu:  "But then... what do we do!?"

730
00:54:02,000 --> 00:54:09,000
Fuyu:  "Mirari's unconscious! She needs somewhere warm to rest, a-and something to eat, and... and...!"

731
00:54:09,000 --> 00:54:15,000
You:  "Calm down, Fuyu! If you panic, you're just going to make things even harder on yourself."

732
00:54:15,000 --> 00:54:19,000
You:  "For the time being, you're both coming back to my cabin."

733
00:54:19,000 --> 00:54:25,000
You:  "I'll help you to carry Mirari back there, and we'll make sure to keep her nice and warm."

734
00:54:25,000 --> 00:54:28,000
Fuyu:  "N... No, but... we couldn't possibly--"

735
00:54:28,000 --> 00:54:30,000
You:  "I wasn't asking!"

736
00:54:30,000 --> 00:54:34,000
You:  "You take one arm, I'll take the other. Got it?"

737
00:54:34,000 --> 00:54:36,000
Fuyu:  "Y... Yes! I understand!"

738
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:39,000
Fuyu:  "If it's for the princess, then...!"

739
00:54:39,000 --> 00:54:43,000
*Fuyu comes to her senses and grabs hold of Mirari tightly.*

740
00:54:43,000 --> 00:54:49,000
*I do the same, grabbing Mirari's other arm and wrapping her arm around my shoulders.*

741
00:54:49,000 --> 00:54:57,000
*Like so, Fuyu and I begin to carry the unconscious princess back to my truck, braving the hellish blizzard once more.*

742
00:54:57,000 --> 00:55:05,000
*Through great exertion, and with much difficulty, I manage to bring Mirari and Fuyu back to my cabin, safe and sound.*

743
00:55:05,000 --> 00:55:14,000
*While the two girls aren't injured, it seems that they're both utterly exhausted, with Mirari still unconscious and likely running a fever.*

744
00:55:14,000 --> 00:55:20,000
*Fuyu is sick with worry, and clearly over-exerting herself, but otherwise appears to be fine.*

745
00:55:20,000 --> 00:55:22,000
You:  "How is Mirari doing?"

746
00:55:22,000 --> 00:55:23,000
You:  "Any change?"

747
00:55:23,000 --> 00:55:26,000
*In response to my question, Fuyu shakes her head.*

748
00:55:26,000 --> 00:55:30,000
Fuyu:  "Still nothing... The princess won't wake up at all."

749
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:31,000
You:  "Ahh, too bad."

750
00:55:31,000 --> 00:55:35,000
You:  "Oh well. Just give her time and she'll be okay."

751
00:55:35,000 --> 00:55:36,000
Fuyu:  "...I hope so."

752
00:55:36,000 --> 00:55:39,000
*Fuyu sulks as she shrugs off my optimism.*

753
00:55:39,000 --> 00:55:44,000
*It seems that her concern for her friend is not so easily dismissed.*

754
00:55:44,000 --> 00:55:48,000
You:  "You know, Mirari was in far worse shape when I found her."

755
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:55,000
You:  "As long as she's kept warm, and given a chance to rest, I think she'll definitely pull through."

756
00:55:55,000 --> 00:55:57,000
You:  "For the time being..."

757
00:55:57,000 --> 00:56:02,000
*Positioning myself directly behind Fuyu, I place one hand on the girl's head.*

758
00:56:02,000 --> 00:56:05,000
You:  "I'm more worried about you, Fuyu."

759
00:56:05,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Fuyu:  "...Me?"

760
00:56:06,000 --> 00:56:09,000
Fuyu:  "Why would you be... worried about me?"

761
00:56:09,000 --> 00:56:11,000
You:  "Is that really so strange?"

762
00:56:11,000 --> 00:56:15,000
You:  "You were out there in that blizzard too, you know."

763
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:25,000
You:  "You even wound up carrying Mirari all by yourself before I got there, not to mention the panic and stress you would have been suffering from."

764
00:56:25,000 --> 00:56:27,000
You:  "So... how are you holding up?"

765
00:56:27,000 --> 00:56:32,000
You:  "Do you need anything, Fuyu? Is there something I can do for you?"

766
00:56:32,000 --> 00:56:34,000
Fuyu:  "D... Don't be absurd."

767
00:56:34,000 --> 00:56:38,000
Fuyu:  "Your concern is entirely unnecessary, human."

768
00:56:38,000 --> 00:56:42,000
*Fuyu pouts and turns away with a red tinge to her cheeks.*

769
00:56:42,000 --> 00:56:46,000
Fuyu:  "...You should focus your attention on Mirari instead."

770
00:56:46,000 --> 00:56:49,000
Fuyu:  "She's the important one here, not me."

771
00:56:49,000 --> 00:56:55,000
Fuyu:  "I would have gladly given my life if it meant bringing her back home, safe and sound."

772
00:56:55,000 --> 00:56:59,000
*I begin to rub Fuyu's head while chuckling to myself.*

773
00:56:59,000 --> 00:57:09,000
You:  "So what you're saying is, you're so concerned for your friend's happiness that you'd give up your own life in order for her to achieve it?"

774
00:57:09,000 --> 00:57:11,000
Fuyu:  "That isn't what I said!"

775
00:57:11,000 --> 00:57:17,000
Fuyu:  "I-I just don't want the pack to suffer because of that girl's selfish whims, that's all!"

776
00:57:17,000 --> 00:57:19,000
You:  "Yes, yes. I understand."

777
00:57:19,000 --> 00:57:22,000
*I continue to pet Fuyu as she sulks.*

778
00:57:22,000 --> 00:57:29,000
*Despite her usual temperament, she doesn't push my hand away, nor does she appear to dislike the contact.*

779
00:57:29,000 --> 00:57:35,000
*If she weren't so proud, she might actually give in to the feeling and lean in closer.*

780
00:57:35,000 --> 00:57:43,000
You:  "...But you know, Fuyu, as great as it is to be loyal, you shouldn't put so little importance on your own life."

781
00:57:43,000 --> 00:57:52,000
You:  "Just as your pack misses Mirari, I'm sure they miss you, too. And I know for a fact that if you were gone, Mirari would be devastated."

782
00:57:52,000 --> 00:57:55,000
You:  "So... don't throw your life away, okay?"

783
00:57:55,000 --> 00:57:59,000
You:  "Take care of yourself, just as you take care of Mirari."

784
00:57:59,000 --> 00:58:02,000
You:  "Right. What am I worrying about?"

785
00:58:02,000 --> 00:58:09,000
You:  "Those girls know this mountain far better than I do. They've probably lived up here their whole lives."

786
00:58:09,000 --> 00:58:17,000
You:  "If they couldn't sense bad weather coming and create makeshift shelter, they'd have probably died long before now."

787
00:58:17,000 --> 00:58:23,000
*Convincing myself thusly, I pick up the remote control and turn on the television.*

788
00:58:23,000 --> 00:58:33,000
*Although there's no TV reception up here, I do have stacks of VHS tapes and DVDs to watch, one of which is still sitting in the player attached to the TV.*

789
00:58:33,000 --> 00:58:41,000
*Without bothering to check what's in there, I hit play, lay back, and allow myself to slowly enter a state of vegetation.*

790
00:58:41,000 --> 00:58:48,000
*As my days pass by in solitude, I often find myself wondering about what happened to Mirari and Fuyu.*

791
00:58:48,000 --> 00:59:02,000
*Those two wolf-girls, who I haven't seen once since they left, remain on my mind for months as I think about what they've been doing since we parted ways, and whether they will ever show up on my door step again.*

792
00:59:02,000 --> 00:59:09,000
*No matter how much time passes, however, those two girls do not return to my cabin. Nobody does.*

793
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:20,000
*Solitude, the one thing I sought in coming here, becomes both my curse and my blessing as I spend every single day in isolation, ignorant of the world outside.*

794
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:25,000
*When Summer rolls around, I head out into the snow in search of firewood.*

795
00:59:25,000 --> 00:59:37,000
*It's an unnecessary task, to be honest. I have electricity and a heater already. Chopping firewood is nothing more than a means by which to spend my boring, uneventful days.*

796
00:59:37,000 --> 00:59:42,000
*One day however, while I'm outside chopping wood, I come across a strange sight.*

797
00:59:42,000 --> 00:59:51,000
*Buried in the snow beneath my feet are rags of cloth - dirty and worn down as if they've survived the elements for untold ages.*

798
00:59:51,000 --> 01:00:02,000
*Curious, I begin to dig into the snow. I toss aside my ax and push away the snow with my gloved hands, convincing myself that I absolutely must see what lies beneath.*

799
01:00:02,000 --> 01:00:06,000
*The moment I'm met with success, I desperately wish I hadn't.*

800
01:00:06,000 --> 01:00:12,000
*Beneath the snow are a white one-piece dress, torn jeans, two collars, and undergarments.*

801
01:00:12,000 --> 01:00:18,000
*The exact outfits Mirari and Fuyu were wearing the day they left my cabin for the last time.*

802
01:00:18,000 --> 01:00:25,000
*After a long night of watching Fuyu fuss over Mirari, I eventually turn in for the night and go to bed.*

803
01:00:25,000 --> 01:00:35,000
*Convincing Fuyu to do the same proves surprisingly difficult. She's adamant about being there for Mirari, and doesn't want to leave her side.*

804
01:00:35,000 --> 01:00:45,000
*It isn't until I convey to Fuyu the expected time at which Mirari will awaken - a complete lie on my part - that Fuyu finally agrees to rest.*

805
01:00:45,000 --> 01:00:54,000
*She snuggles up next to Mirari, just as they had when they slept on the couch together previously, and before long, Fuyu is sound asleep.*

806
01:00:54,000 --> 01:00:57,000
*(Sheesh. Those two really are a handful.)*

807
01:00:57,000 --> 01:01:03,000
*(Maybe I shouldn't get a pet after all? Looking after those two is already tiring enough.)*

808
01:01:03,000 --> 01:01:07,000
You:  "Well, I guess I'd better go see how the two are doing."

809
01:01:07,000 --> 01:01:10,000
You:  "If I'm lucky, maybe they'll have slept in."

810
01:01:10,000 --> 01:01:18,000
*Despite my optimism, the very first thing I see upon entering the living room is the sight of Fuyu towering over Mirari.*

811
01:01:18,000 --> 01:01:21,000
Mirari:  "I-I mean it, I'm feeling much better now."

812
01:01:21,000 --> 01:01:24,000
Mirari:  "Really, I can get up on my own."

813
01:01:24,000 --> 01:01:28,000
Fuyu:  "I don't care if you're feeling better. No means no!"

814
01:01:28,000 --> 01:01:32,000
Fuyu:  "You're going to stay in bed and rest. Got it?"

815
01:01:32,000 --> 01:01:35,000
Mirari:  "No, but... What about breakfast?"

816
01:01:35,000 --> 01:01:37,000
Fuyu:  "{i}I'll{/i} make breakfast."

817
01:01:37,000 --> 01:01:42,000
Fuyu:  "You just keep resting until I bring your portion over to you."

818
01:01:42,000 --> 01:01:45,000
Mirari:  "...Would that really be alright?"

819
01:01:45,000 --> 01:01:49,000
Mirari:  "You haven't received the same training that I have."

820
01:01:49,000 --> 01:01:53,000
Fuyu:  "Hmph. Don't you worry about me. It'll be a piece of cake!"

821
01:01:53,000 --> 01:01:56,000
Fuyu:  "How hard can human cuisine be anyway?"

822
01:01:56,000 --> 01:02:02,000
Fuyu:  "If [player_name] can make it, then there's no way that someone like me won't be able to."

823
01:02:02,000 --> 01:02:03,000
You:  "Oh really?"

824
01:02:03,000 --> 01:02:06,000
You:  "That's quite the declaration there, Fuyu."

825
01:02:06,000 --> 01:02:09,000
*Fuyu freezes up the moment she hears my voice.*

826
01:02:09,000 --> 01:02:16,000
*With great hesitation, Fuyu slowly turns her head until she's looking at me out of the corner of her eye.*

827
01:02:16,000 --> 01:02:20,000
Fuyu:  "[player_name]... H-How long have you been standing there?"

828
01:02:20,000 --> 01:02:25,000
You:  "Long enough to hear you promise that you'll be making us all breakfast."

829
01:02:25,000 --> 01:02:29,000
You:  "Do you need me to show you where the storeroom is?"

830
01:02:29,000 --> 01:02:31,000
Fuyu:  "Uhm... W-Well..."

831
01:02:31,000 --> 01:02:35,000
*Fuyu averts her gaze as she tries to avoid my question.*

832
01:02:35,000 --> 01:02:42,000
*It seems this rowdy wolf-girl doesn't possess her princess's knowledge of such things after all.*

833
01:02:42,000 --> 01:02:44,000
Mirari:  "[player_name]!"

834
01:02:44,000 --> 01:02:50,000
*Before I can tease Fuyu any further, Mirari calls out to me in a surprisingly assertive voice.*

835
01:02:50,000 --> 01:02:51,000
You:  "Y-Yes, Mirari?"

836
01:02:51,000 --> 01:02:52,000
Mirari:  "......"

837
01:02:52,000 --> 01:02:54,000
Mirari:  "[player_name], I..."

838
01:02:54,000 --> 01:02:56,000
Mirari:  "I apologize."

839
01:02:56,000 --> 01:02:57,000
You:  "...Huh?"

840
01:02:57,000 --> 01:02:59,000
Fuyu:  "P... Princess...?"

841
01:02:59,000 --> 01:03:04,000
*Fuyu and I both stare at Mirari in surprise as she hangs her head.*

842
01:03:04,000 --> 01:03:13,000
Mirari:  "Even after you told me to leave... even after I resolved myself to stop relying on your kindness... here I am once again."

843
01:03:13,000 --> 01:03:21,000
Mirari:  "I've burdened you once more, forcing you to take care of me even after you've already done so much for me."

844
01:03:21,000 --> 01:03:25,000
Mirari:  "I... I just want you to know that... this is it."

845
01:03:25,000 --> 01:03:30,000
Mirari:  "As soon as I am able, I will leave this cabin and never come back."

846
01:03:30,000 --> 01:03:33,000
Mirari:  "I will... not bother you ever again."

847
01:03:33,000 --> 01:03:34,000
Fuyu:  "Princess..."

848
01:03:34,000 --> 01:03:42,000
*Despite the fact that Mirari is now agreeing to leave without a fight, even Fuyu can't accept her downhearted proclamation.*

849
01:03:42,000 --> 01:03:50,000
*If Mirari had been able to declare with a smile on her face that she would return to her pack, I would wish her well.*

850
01:03:50,000 --> 01:03:56,000
*Fuyu would happily lead her along, the duo would return home, and that would be the end of it.*

851
01:03:56,000 --> 01:03:59,000
*Given Mirari's current state of mind, however--*

852
01:03:59,000 --> 01:04:02,000
You:  "Think before you speak, Mirari."

853
01:04:02,000 --> 01:04:08,000
You:  "If you say something that stupid, there's no way I'm going to let you leave."

854
01:04:08,000 --> 01:04:09,000
Fuyu:  "......"

855
01:04:09,000 --> 01:04:11,000
Mirari:  "...[player_name]...?"

856
01:04:11,000 --> 01:04:18,000
You:  "Listen to me, Mirari. This is twice now that you've almost died because you've gone out unprepared."

857
01:04:18,000 --> 01:04:26,000
You:  "The weather's been unpredictable lately. The paths have changed, and half of the snow underfoot is unstable."

858
01:04:26,000 --> 01:04:32,000
You:  "I'm not going to be held responsible for you running off to your death, Mirari. So..."

859
01:04:32,000 --> 01:04:38,000
You:  "Until I say otherwise, the two of you are staying right here with me. Got it?"

860
01:04:38,000 --> 01:04:39,000
Fuyu:  "......"

861
01:04:39,000 --> 01:04:40,000
Mirari:  "......"

862
01:04:40,000 --> 01:04:42,000
Fuyu:  "Y-You mean that..."

863
01:04:42,000 --> 01:04:44,000
Mirari:  "...We can stay?"

864
01:04:44,000 --> 01:04:46,000
*I nod in confirmation.*

865
01:04:46,000 --> 01:04:49,000
Fuyu:  "P-Princess, did you hear that?"

866
01:04:49,000 --> 01:04:52,000
Mirari:  "We can stay! We can stay here after all!"

867
01:04:52,000 --> 01:04:54,000
Mirari:  "Oh, this is such a relief!"

868
01:04:54,000 --> 01:04:56,000
Fuyu:  "Yes, princess, I'm also--"

869
01:04:56,000 --> 01:05:00,000
Fuyu:  "I-I mean, I'm happy for {i}you{/i}, princess."

870
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:08,000
Fuyu:  "If you must linger awhile for the sake of your recovery, th-then I have no choice but to keep you company."

871
01:05:08,000 --> 01:05:14,000
*The two girls join hands and bounce on their heels, wearing expressions of joy as they do.*

872
01:05:14,000 --> 01:05:19,000
*Contrary to Fuyu's words, it seems she's just as relieved as Mirari.*

873
01:05:19,000 --> 01:05:21,000
*(You're so transparent, Fuyu.)*

874
01:05:21,000 --> 01:05:29,000
*(Can't you just honestly say that you don't know how to get home, and you're afraid of putting Mirari in danger again?)*

875
01:05:29,000 --> 01:05:33,000
*Chuckling to myself, I move closer to the two girls.*

876
01:05:33,000 --> 01:05:40,000
You:  "Remember, this is just until the weather clears up, and you're able to make your way back home."

877
01:05:40,000 --> 01:05:48,000
You:  "I'll be listening to the radio every day for any mention of the snow being cleared away, or the weather improving."

878
01:05:48,000 --> 01:05:53,000
Mirari:  "U-Understood! We shan't overstay our welcome a second time."

879
01:05:53,000 --> 01:05:57,000
Mirari:  "When the time is right, we'll leave without a fuss."

880
01:05:57,000 --> 01:06:02,000
*By the time noon has rolled around, the weather outside seems to have improved.*

881
01:06:02,000 --> 01:06:12,000
*Not to the point where I have any confidence in making a long trek, but at the very least it seems as though I'll be able to scout out the area.*

882
01:06:12,000 --> 01:06:17,000
*(Alright, I should take this opportunity to check out the new landscape.)*

883
01:06:17,000 --> 01:06:24,000
*(In particular, I'll see if the path Mirari and Fuyu were taking yesterday has cleared up at all.)*

884
01:06:24,000 --> 01:06:33,000
*After confirming on the radio that the weather is set to remain unchanged for the rest of the day, I begin to put on my boots and coat.*

885
01:06:33,000 --> 01:06:35,000
Mirari:  "[player_name]...?"

886
01:06:35,000 --> 01:06:37,000
Mirari:  "Where are you going?"

887
01:06:37,000 --> 01:06:38,000
You:  "Oh, Mirari."

888
01:06:38,000 --> 01:06:45,000
You:  "I was just going to go check out the terrain, now that the weather has stabilized for a bit."

889
01:06:45,000 --> 01:06:47,000
You:  "I'll be back before long."

890
01:06:47,000 --> 01:06:49,000
Mirari:  "I-I'll come with you!"

891
01:06:49,000 --> 01:06:50,000
You:  "No, you won't."

892
01:06:50,000 --> 01:06:56,000
*I gently flick Mirari on the forehead as if to punish her for saying something unreasonable.*

893
01:06:56,000 --> 01:07:01,000
You:  "You just stay put and recover. I don't want you over-exerting yourself."

894
01:07:01,000 --> 01:07:06,000
Mirari:  "But I... I can't just continue to leech off your kindness like this."

895
01:07:06,000 --> 01:07:13,000
Mirari:  "I need to make myself useful. It's the least I can do, considering everything you're doing for me."

896
01:07:13,000 --> 01:07:21,000
You:  "I appreciate your feelings, but if you come with me and you faint again, you're only going to cause more trouble."

897
01:07:21,000 --> 01:07:23,000
Mirari:  "{i}Uuu...{/i}"

898
01:07:23,000 --> 01:07:28,000
*Mirari sulks as I point out the major flaw in her offer without hesitation.*

899
01:07:28,000 --> 01:07:30,000
You:  "{i}sigh...{/i} Listen, uhm..."

900
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:39,000
You:  "I know it's kind of rude to ask this of a sick person, and I'm not implying that this is all you're good for or anything, but..."

901
01:07:39,000 --> 01:07:47,000
You:  "If you're really itching for something to do, why don't you clean up a bit, or make lunch for when I get back?"

902
01:07:47,000 --> 01:07:50,000
You:  "Only if you're feeling up to it, of course."

903
01:07:50,000 --> 01:07:52,000
Mirari:  "Y... Yes! Absolutely!"

904
01:07:52,000 --> 01:07:56,000
Mirari:  "It would be my pleasure, [player_name]! Thank you!"

905
01:07:56,000 --> 01:08:01,000
You:  "No... You really don't need to thank me for assigning you chores."

906
01:08:01,000 --> 01:08:08,000
*Without wasting a moment, Mirari skips over to the storeroom, where I keep all of the cleaning supplies.*

907
01:08:08,000 --> 01:08:13,000
*It seems the specter of illness means nothing to Mirari after all.*

908
01:08:13,000 --> 01:08:16,000
*Dressed suitably, I head out into the snow.*

909
01:08:16,000 --> 01:08:21,000
*As I go to close the door behind me, however, I feel something block my way.*

910
01:08:21,000 --> 01:08:24,000
Fuyu:  "Hey, watch it, [player_name]."

911
01:08:24,000 --> 01:08:26,000
You:  "Oh, I'm sorry, Fuyu."

912
01:08:26,000 --> 01:08:30,000
*Fuyu pushes past me, and this time I close the door for real.*

913
01:08:30,000 --> 01:08:32,000
You:  "...Wait a minute."

914
01:08:32,000 --> 01:08:35,000
You:  "What are you doing out here, Fuyu?"

915
01:08:35,000 --> 01:08:39,000
Fuyu:  "What? Do I need your permission to go outside?"

916
01:08:39,000 --> 01:08:41,000
You:  "Well... no. I guess not."

917
01:08:41,000 --> 01:08:45,000
You:  "But given the timing, it's like you were following--"

918
01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:53,000
Fuyu:  "Y-You're going to check out the terrain, aren't you? To see what's changed, and where you can get through?"

919
01:08:53,000 --> 01:09:03,000
Fuyu:  "If you're going to try to reach our den, then you'll need a guide. And I can hardly allow the princess to go, given her current condition."

920
01:09:03,000 --> 01:09:07,000
You:  "...I never said anything about visiting your "den"."

921
01:09:07,000 --> 01:09:10,000
You:  "{i}sigh...{/i} Fine. You can come along."

922
01:09:10,000 --> 01:09:12,000
You:  "Just don't get too far--"

923
01:09:12,000 --> 01:09:13,000
You:  "...Ahead."

924
01:09:13,000 --> 01:09:16,000
*Fuyu runs off before I can finish speaking.*

925
01:09:16,000 --> 01:09:20,000
You:  "Oh well. If she's this lively, it shouldn't be a problem."

926
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
You:  "Besides, I {i}was{/i} planning on checking out the path those girls took yesterday."

927
01:09:26,000 --> 01:09:32,000
You:  "I guess the only change of plans is that I'll now be doing it with company."

928
01:09:32,000 --> 01:09:38,000
*Following after Fuyu, I soon reach the stretch of snow where I found the two girls yesterday.*

929
01:09:38,000 --> 01:09:43,000
*While visibility has certainly improved, the path itself is still blocked off.*

930
01:09:43,000 --> 01:09:47,000
*At a glance, it doesn't seem like there's any way to get through.*

931
01:09:47,000 --> 01:09:49,000
Fuyu:  "Still no good, huh?"

932
01:09:49,000 --> 01:09:50,000
Fuyu:  "Maybe if I..."

933
01:09:50,000 --> 01:09:52,000
Fuyu:  "No, that won't work."

934
01:09:52,000 --> 01:10:00,000
You:  "I hate to break it to you, Fuyu, but it doesn't look like you'll be getting through here. Not today, at least."

935
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:02,000
Fuyu:  "Mmm... I know."

936
01:10:02,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Fuyu:  "Even so, I can't just give up and return empty-handed."

937
01:10:06,000 --> 01:10:11,000
Fuyu:  "What would the princess say if I returned without securing a route home?"

938
01:10:11,000 --> 01:10:13,000
You:  "She'd probably be relieved."

939
01:10:13,000 --> 01:10:19,000
You:  "You may want to go back as soon as possible, but I get the feeling Mirari isn't so keen."

940
01:10:19,000 --> 01:10:25,000
Fuyu:  "...Whether she wants to return or not, the princess understands that we must."

941
01:10:25,000 --> 01:10:30,000
Fuyu:  "As such, it is my duty to ensure that return is made possible."

942
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:39,000
You:  "Well, good luck with that. Unless you have a snow plough handy, I don't think you'll be getting through here any time soon."

943
01:10:39,000 --> 01:10:40,000
Fuyu:  "...Hmm..."

944
01:10:40,000 --> 01:10:44,000
Fuyu:  "{i}*scratch* *scratch* *scratch* *scratch*{/i}"

945
01:10:44,000 --> 01:10:48,000
You:  "Fuyu, you {i}cannot{/i} dig your way through."

946
01:10:48,000 --> 01:10:50,000
Fuyu:  "Not with that attitude!"

947
01:10:50,000 --> 01:10:54,000
Fuyu:  "{i}*scratch* *scratch* *scratch* *scratch*{/i}"

948
01:10:54,000 --> 01:10:56,000
You:  "{i}sigh...{/i} Seriously?"

949
01:10:56,000 --> 01:11:05,000
You:  "At least wait for the snow to melt a bit. Trying to dig through there right now must be like clawing your way through stone."

950
01:11:05,000 --> 01:11:08,000
Fuyu:  "Hmph. Don't underestimate the might of--"

951
01:11:08,000 --> 01:11:09,000
Fuyu:  "Funyah!!?"

952
01:11:09,000 --> 01:11:14,000
*Fuyu suddenly jumps up in fright as some of the piled-up snow falls onto her.*

953
01:11:14,000 --> 01:11:21,000
*It seems that having Fuyu dig at the base of the snow has caused it to shift under its own weight.*

954
01:11:21,000 --> 01:11:24,000
You:  "Hahahaha... A-Are you alright, Fuyu?"

955
01:11:24,000 --> 01:11:27,000
Fuyu:  "{i}Uuu...{/i} Don't laugh at me, human!"

956
01:11:27,000 --> 01:11:31,000
You:  "Sorry, sorry. It's just, the way you shrieked like that--"

957
01:11:31,000 --> 01:11:32,000
You:  "Woah!"

958
01:11:32,000 --> 01:11:36,000
*I dodge at the last second as a snowball narrowly misses my head.*

959
01:11:36,000 --> 01:11:40,000
You:  "What are you doing, Fuyu!? You could have hit me!"

960
01:11:40,000 --> 01:11:42,000
Fuyu:  "That's the point, you fool!"

961
01:11:42,000 --> 01:11:43,000
*{i}*fwoosh*{/i}*

962
01:11:43,000 --> 01:11:44,000
You:  "Uwah!"

963
01:11:44,000 --> 01:11:49,000
*Fuyu's second snowball clips my shoulder, knocking me off-balance.*

964
01:11:49,000 --> 01:11:50,000
You:  "You little...!"

965
01:11:50,000 --> 01:11:52,000
Fuyu:  "Nya-nya! Stupid human."

966
01:11:52,000 --> 01:11:56,000
Fuyu:  "That's what you get for making fun of-- Hyah!?"

967
01:11:56,000 --> 01:12:04,000
*Without rising to my feet, I quickly ball up some snow and hurl it towards Fuyu, just barely missing her torso.*

968
01:12:04,000 --> 01:12:08,000
Fuyu:  "Wh-What the heck do you think you're doing!?"

969
01:12:08,000 --> 01:12:11,000
You:  "Throwing a snowball. What does it look like?"

970
01:12:11,000 --> 01:12:16,000
Fuyu:  "You can't do that! I'm the one throwing snow at {i}you{/i}!"

971
01:12:16,000 --> 01:12:18,000
You:  "What are you, a little kid?"

972
01:12:18,000 --> 01:12:22,000
You:  "I don't need your permission to defend myself."

973
01:12:22,000 --> 01:12:23,000
You:  "Hup!"

974
01:12:23,000 --> 01:12:26,000
Fuyu:  "Kyah! S-Stop that right this instant!"

975
01:12:26,000 --> 01:12:27,000
You:  "Make me."

976
01:12:27,000 --> 01:12:28,000
Fuyu:  "Grrr...!"

977
01:12:28,000 --> 01:12:33,000
Fuyu:  "Fine then! We'll see how you like it when I throw a snowball at you!"

978
01:12:33,000 --> 01:12:37,000
You:  "Well, yeah. That's how this fight started-- Woah!"

979
01:12:37,000 --> 01:12:41,000
*I duck to the side as Fuyu throws another snowball at my head.*

980
01:12:41,000 --> 01:12:49,000
*The moment I correct my posture, Fuyu has already started to ball up another, and she's getting ready to throw it.*

981
01:12:49,000 --> 01:12:53,000
You:  "Sheesh, give me a break! How can you do that so quickly?"

982
01:12:53,000 --> 01:13:00,000
Fuyu:  "Hmph. Someone who wears those ridiculous things on their hands will never be able to match my speed."

983
01:13:00,000 --> 01:13:03,000
You:  "Oh yeah? We'll see about that!"

984
01:13:03,000 --> 01:13:04,000
You:  "Hup!"

985
01:13:04,000 --> 01:13:06,000
Fuyu:  "Nyahaha~ Too slow~"

986
01:13:06,000 --> 01:13:09,000
Fuyu:  "Should I give you a handicap, human?"

987
01:13:09,000 --> 01:13:11,000
You:  "Don't underestimate me!"

988
01:13:11,000 --> 01:13:19,000
*Before I realize it, I find myself becoming more and more invested in the outcome of my snowball fight with Fuyu.*

989
01:13:19,000 --> 01:13:29,000
*What starts as a cheeky bit of fun quickly develops into an intense showdown, with both sides putting in far more effort than one would expect.*

990
01:13:29,000 --> 01:13:33,000
*As strange as it may seem, I'm actually having fun.*

991
01:13:33,000 --> 01:13:43,000
*(Spending every day out here, struggling to stay warm and keep my supplies up, I sometimes forget about the upsides of being surrounded by snow.)*

992
01:13:43,000 --> 01:13:54,000
*(When was the last time I even {i}thought{/i} about having a snowball fight? Or making snow angels? Or engaging in any of those fun yet childish activities?)*

993
01:13:54,000 --> 01:14:00,000
*(Maybe this place doesn't have to be the barren wasteland I always think of it as after all.)*

994
01:14:00,000 --> 01:14:02,000
Fuyu:  "Kyahaha! Missed me!"

995
01:14:02,000 --> 01:14:04,000
You:  "Grr... Stop moving!"

996
01:14:04,000 --> 01:14:06,000
Fuyu:  "Not gonna happen~"

997
01:14:06,000 --> 01:14:11,000
*Fuyu turns around and wiggles her butt in my direction, mocking me.*

998
01:14:11,000 --> 01:14:18,000
*At that moment, I reveal a second snowball hidden behind my back and throw it as quickly as I can.*

999
01:14:18,000 --> 01:14:19,000
Fuyu:  "Kyaa!?"

1000
01:14:19,000 --> 01:14:20,000
You:  "Gotcha!"

1001
01:14:20,000 --> 01:14:23,000
Fuyu:  "Ooh... D-Did you have to throw it there?"

1002
01:14:23,000 --> 01:14:27,000
Fuyu:  "The snow is dripping into my pants. It's really cold!"

1003
01:14:27,000 --> 01:14:33,000
You:  "So wear proper clothing next time. It's not my fault you're dressed like that."

1004
01:14:33,000 --> 01:14:39,000
*Fuyu dances around, trying to shift the snow that has trickled under her clothes.*

1005
01:14:39,000 --> 01:14:46,000
*A few small pieces of snow fall out, but judging by the expression on her face, there's still more to come.*

1006
01:14:46,000 --> 01:14:47,000
You:  "Chance!"

1007
01:14:47,000 --> 01:14:48,000
Fuyu:  "Uwah!?"

1008
01:14:48,000 --> 01:14:53,000
Fuyu:  "Wh-What are you doing!? Can't you see that I'm preoccupied?"

1009
01:14:53,000 --> 01:14:57,000
You:  "That's exactly what makes it such a perfect opportunity."

1010
01:14:57,000 --> 01:14:58,000
You:  "Hup!"

1011
01:14:58,000 --> 01:14:59,000
Fuyu:  "Yah! Stop it!"

1012
01:14:59,000 --> 01:15:00,000
You:  "Make me."

1013
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:01,000
Fuyu:  "Yahahaha~"

1014
01:15:01,000 --> 01:15:07,000
*Despite her complaints, Fuyu laughs happily as she dodges my opportunistic onslaught.*

1015
01:15:07,000 --> 01:15:15,000
*Dodging while simultaneously removing snow from under her clothes, Fuyu displays dexterity I could only dream of possessing.*

1016
01:15:15,000 --> 01:15:18,000
Fuyu:  "And... there! That's the last of it."

1017
01:15:18,000 --> 01:15:22,000
Fuyu:  "You'd better prepare yourself now, [player_name]!"

1018
01:15:22,000 --> 01:15:30,000
*Grinning from ear to ear, a playful smile adorns Fuyu's face as she hurriedly begins to create another snowball.*

1019
01:15:30,000 --> 01:15:34,000
*No matter what she says, it's clear to me that she's having fun.*

1020
01:15:34,000 --> 01:15:39,000
*(Fuyu may be abrasive and direct, but it looks like even she has a fun side.)*

1021
01:15:39,000 --> 01:15:45,000
*(She's also pretty cute when she smiles, and it's evident that she cares deeply about Mirari.)*

1022
01:15:45,000 --> 01:15:49,000
*(My first impression of Fuyu might have been wrong after all.)*

1023
01:15:49,000 --> 01:15:57,000
*(If Fuyu were just a little bit more honest, and less defensive, she might actually make a pretty good housemate.)*

1024
01:15:57,000 --> 01:16:03,000
*Upon returning to the cabin, Fuyu and I are greeted by the delicious smell of home cooking.*

1025
01:16:03,000 --> 01:16:09,000
*Awaiting us in the kitchen is Mirari, who seems to have just finished cooking as we return.*

1026
01:16:09,000 --> 01:16:17,000
*Without wasting any time, Mirari greets the two of us, places three bowls on the table, and invites us over to eat.*

1027
01:16:17,000 --> 01:16:19,000
Fuyu:  "Mmmm! This is sooo good!"

1028
01:16:19,000 --> 01:16:23,000
Fuyu:  "Nothing like a hot meal after playing around in the snow."

1029
01:16:23,000 --> 01:16:25,000
Mirari:  "Playing around?"

1030
01:16:25,000 --> 01:16:30,000
Mirari:  "I thought the two of you were going to check the terrain?"

1031
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:34,000
Fuyu:  "A-Ah... Uhm... No, I wasn't "playing" exactly..."

1032
01:16:34,000 --> 01:16:37,000
Fuyu:  "It was more like... a grudge match?"

1033
01:16:37,000 --> 01:16:39,000
Mirari:  "A-A grudge match!?"

1034
01:16:39,000 --> 01:16:41,000
Mirari:  "Between whom?"

1035
01:16:41,000 --> 01:16:45,000
You:  "Relax, Mirari. That's just Fuyu acting tough."

1036
01:16:45,000 --> 01:16:49,000
You:  "We were having a snowball fight, that's-- Mmph mmm mmmph."

1037
01:16:49,000 --> 01:16:51,000
Fuyu:  "E-E-Enough out of you!"

1038
01:16:51,000 --> 01:16:53,000
*Fuyu covers my mouth in a fluster.*

1039
01:16:53,000 --> 01:16:57,000
*Unfortunately for Fuyu, she's already far too late.*

1040
01:16:57,000 --> 01:16:59,000
Mirari:  "A snowball fight?"

1041
01:16:59,000 --> 01:17:03,000
Mirari:  "How marvelous! Oh, how I wish I could have joined you."

1042
01:17:03,000 --> 01:17:07,000
*I pull Fuyu's hands away from my mouth and smile wryly at Mirari.*

1043
01:17:07,000 --> 01:17:11,000
You:  "Sorry. We didn't mean to go off and have fun without you."

1044
01:17:11,000 --> 01:17:14,000
Mirari:  "Oh, no. I'm not blaming you."

1045
01:17:14,000 --> 01:17:19,000
Mirari:  "In fact, I'm pleased to see the two of you getting along so well."

1046
01:17:19,000 --> 01:17:22,000
Fuyu:  "G-Getting along!? Who's getting along!?"

1047
01:17:22,000 --> 01:17:26,000
Fuyu:  "I was simply defending my honor, that's all!"

1048
01:17:26,000 --> 01:17:27,000
Fuyu:  "Bleugh!"

1049
01:17:27,000 --> 01:17:32,000
*Fuyu sticks her tongue out towards me, then returns to eating her lunch.*

1050
01:17:32,000 --> 01:17:36,000
*Sighing in defeat, I pick up my fork and start to do the same.*

1051
01:17:36,000 --> 01:17:40,000
*After taking a few bites, I realize that I'm being watched.*

1052
01:17:40,000 --> 01:17:49,000
*As I raise my head, I find that Mirari still isn't eating. Instead, she's simply watching me eat with a satisfied look on her face.*

1053
01:17:49,000 --> 01:17:52,000
You:  "Aren't you going to eat as well?"

1054
01:17:52,000 --> 01:17:56,000
You:  "It can't be that interesting to just watch us eat."

1055
01:17:56,000 --> 01:17:58,000
Mirari:  "Oh, but it is!"

1056
01:17:58,000 --> 01:18:02,000
Mirari:  "It brings me great joy to watch others enjoy my cooking."

1057
01:18:02,000 --> 01:18:04,000
You:  "Is that right...?"

1058
01:18:04,000 --> 01:18:06,000
You:  "Do you cook for others often?"

1059
01:18:06,000 --> 01:18:08,000
Mirari:  "No... I'm afraid not."

1060
01:18:08,000 --> 01:18:14,000
Mirari:  "I've been practicing for years, but it's rare for me to get the chance to feed anyone."

1061
01:18:14,000 --> 01:18:19,000
You:  "Oh, right. You said something about undergoing training before."

1062
01:18:19,000 --> 01:18:26,000
You:  "But if you never get the opportunity to put your skills to use, what's the point in training?"

1063
01:18:26,000 --> 01:18:27,000
Mirari:  "......"

1064
01:18:27,000 --> 01:18:30,000
Mirari:  "They will... be put to use."

1065
01:18:30,000 --> 01:18:32,000
You:  "Really? When will that--"

1066
01:18:32,000 --> 01:18:33,000
Fuyu:  "Seconds!"

1067
01:18:33,000 --> 01:18:38,000
*Before I can finish speaking, Fuyu thrusts her bowl between Mirari and I.*

1068
01:18:38,000 --> 01:18:47,000
*As I glance at the bowl, I realize that there's still a small amount of food left on the bottom, and Fuyu is chewing as she speaks.*

1069
01:18:47,000 --> 01:18:49,000
Mirari:  "O-Oh, yes. Right away!"

1070
01:18:49,000 --> 01:18:52,000
Mirari:  "Gosh, Fuyu. You're never full, are you?"

1071
01:18:52,000 --> 01:18:57,000
Fuyu:  "Nope! I need all of the energy I can get in order to do my job."

1072
01:18:57,000 --> 01:19:01,000
Fuyu:  "So feed me well, princess. It's for your own benefit."

1073
01:19:01,000 --> 01:19:05,000
Mirari:  "Heehee~ Of course. I'll get right on that."

1074
01:19:05,000 --> 01:19:15,000
*Watching the conveniently timed interaction between the two, I realize that Mirari doesn't want to talk about the subject we were discussing any further.*

1075
01:19:15,000 --> 01:19:18,000
*And for my part, I'm happy to drop the matter.*

1076
01:19:18,000 --> 01:19:27,000
*I don't need to know every aspect of these girls' lives. If there are things they don't want to tell me, then that's perfectly fine.*

1077
01:19:27,000 --> 01:19:33,000
*As long as the three of us can get along together, the finer details can be happily forgotten.*

1078
01:19:33,000 --> 01:19:42,000
*Shortly after the girls and I finish eating lunch, I sit down with the two of them and face them with a serious look on my face.*

1079
01:19:42,000 --> 01:19:52,000
*For all of my optimistic thoughts about the three of us getting along without sweating the details, there is one matter which we must still discuss.*

1080
01:19:52,000 --> 01:19:56,000
You:  "Alright, girls. It's time to talk about your plan."

1081
01:19:56,000 --> 01:19:57,000
Mirari:  "Mmm...?"

1082
01:19:57,000 --> 01:19:58,000
Mirari:  "Our plan?"

1083
01:19:58,000 --> 01:20:00,000
Fuyu:  "Our plan for what?"

1084
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:04,000
*Both wolf-girls tilt their heads in unison at my vague question.*

1085
01:20:04,000 --> 01:20:07,000
You:  "...Your plan to get {i}home{/i}."

1086
01:20:07,000 --> 01:20:15,000
You:  "It may not be possible to get through right now, but you're going to need some kind of idea on how to get back home."

1087
01:20:15,000 --> 01:20:23,000
You:  "I mean, I won't tell you to get out right this minute, but surely you aren't planning on staying here forever?"

1088
01:20:23,000 --> 01:20:28,000
Fuyu:  "Hmph! Of course not. Who would want to stay in this human cabin?"

1089
01:20:28,000 --> 01:20:33,000
Fuyu:  "Rest assured, princess. I'll find a way to get us back home in no time."

1090
01:20:33,000 --> 01:20:34,000
Mirari:  "......"

1091
01:20:34,000 --> 01:20:37,000
Mirari:  "Is it really necessary for us to go back?"

1092
01:20:37,000 --> 01:20:45,000
Fuyu:  "Hmm, let's see. I only know the one path over to this side of the mountain, but there are sure to be others."

1093
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:53,000
Fuyu:  "I guess I should start to go out scouting for a little while each day and familiarize myself with the area."

1094
01:20:53,000 --> 01:20:56,000
Fuyu:  "Human, how well do you know this area?"

1095
01:20:56,000 --> 01:21:04,000
You:  "A week ago, I would have said I knew it well. But after the weather we've had recently, I can't really say."

1096
01:21:04,000 --> 01:21:05,000
Mirari:  "......"

1097
01:21:05,000 --> 01:21:08,000
Fuyu:  "Hmm, so the human is useless, as expected."

1098
01:21:08,000 --> 01:21:11,000
Fuyu:  "I guess it's up to me after all!"

1099
01:21:11,000 --> 01:21:15,000
You:  "You're quite a rude little girl, you know that?"

1100
01:21:15,000 --> 01:21:25,000
*Paying no mind to Mirari's sullen mood, Fuyu and I continue to talk about the landscape surrounding us, and possible paths back to the girls' den.*

1101
01:21:25,000 --> 01:21:35,000
*Unfortunately, our talk is for naught. With so much having changed in such a short period of time, my knowledge of the area is useless, and so is my map.*

1102
01:21:35,000 --> 01:21:38,000
*For the time being, all we can do is sit tight.*

1103
01:21:38,000 --> 01:21:42,000
*As night rolls around, I decide that it's time to take a bath.*

1104
01:21:42,000 --> 01:21:50,000
*Thankfully, while drinking water isn't exactly abundant out here, there's no shortage of water suitable for bathing.*

1105
01:21:50,000 --> 01:21:55,000
*Grab some snow, wait for it to melt, filter it, and you have a cold shower.*

1106
01:21:55,000 --> 01:21:58,000
You:  "Alright, I'm going in for a bath."

1107
01:21:58,000 --> 01:22:02,000
You:  "Don't do anything bad while I'm busy bathing."

1108
01:22:02,000 --> 01:22:04,000
Fuyu:  "What are you accusing us of?"

1109
01:22:04,000 --> 01:22:08,000
Fuyu:  "Just go and clean yourself already, smelly human."

1110
01:22:08,000 --> 01:22:11,000
*(Well, I can't say I didn't ask for that.)*

1111
01:22:11,000 --> 01:22:16,000
*Having grabbed a change of clothes and a towel, I head into the bathroom.*

1112
01:22:16,000 --> 01:22:21,000
*I run the water for a few seconds in order to give it time to warm up.*

1113
01:22:21,000 --> 01:22:26,000
*While it's doing that, I strip down and prepare to enter the bath tub.*

1114
01:22:26,000 --> 01:22:30,000
*(Ahh. A warm bath in the middle of a frozen wasteland.)*

1115
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:34,000
*(As far as guilty pleasures go, this one is pretty hard to beat.)*

1116
01:22:34,000 --> 01:22:41,000
*I sink into the bathtub and let out a deep sigh as the water slowly covers more and more of my body.*

1117
01:22:41,000 --> 01:22:46,000
*(Hmm... Come to think of it, I wonder if the wolf-girls use baths like this?)*

1118
01:22:46,000 --> 01:22:52,000
*(Mirari seems to know her way around a house, so it wouldn't surprise me if she did.)*

1119
01:22:52,000 --> 01:22:59,000
*(Fuyu, on the other hand... I could totally see her licking herself clean in the middle of the living room.)*

1120
01:22:59,000 --> 01:23:00,000
You:  "......"

1121
01:23:00,000 --> 01:23:05,000
*(No, no, no! Do {i}not{/i} picture that. Don't picture either of those things.)*

1122
01:23:05,000 --> 01:23:10,000
*(Those girls are guests in this house. I can't be thinking of them that way.)*

1123
01:23:10,000 --> 01:23:14,000
*My expression falls as I think about the girls' situation.*

1124
01:23:14,000 --> 01:23:23,000
*While I'm willing to let them stay with me if it's just for a little while, I understand that I'm ultimately doing them no favors.*

1125
01:23:23,000 --> 01:23:28,000
*(If I kick them out now, they'll likely freeze to death, or die of starvation.)*

1126
01:23:28,000 --> 01:23:36,000
*(But if I let them stay too long, they'll wind up getting used to life here, and they'll become unable to rejoin their pack.)*

1127
01:23:36,000 --> 01:23:39,000
*(...This is a surprisingly delicate matter.)*

1128
01:23:39,000 --> 01:23:40,000
*{i}*squeak*{/i}*

1129
01:23:40,000 --> 01:23:41,000
You:  "Hmm?"

1130
01:23:41,000 --> 01:23:47,000
*Before I can sink too deeply into my own thoughts, an unexpected sound reaches my ears.*

1131
01:23:47,000 --> 01:23:51,000
*As I turn to see what caused the disturbance, what I find is--*

1132
01:23:51,000 --> 01:23:52,000
You:  "...M-Mirari?"

1133
01:23:52,000 --> 01:23:53,000
Mirari:  "......"

1134
01:23:53,000 --> 01:23:58,000
*Mirari averts her gaze as she walks towards me, clad in nothing but a towel.*

1135
01:23:58,000 --> 01:24:01,000
You:  "M-Mirari, what are you doing in here?"

1136
01:24:01,000 --> 01:24:05,000
You:  "If you want to take a bath, you can do so after I finish."

1137
01:24:05,000 --> 01:24:10,000
*I lean forward in order to cover up as Mirari continues to come closer.*

1138
01:24:10,000 --> 01:24:17,000
*The moment I do, Mirari slips into the bathtub behind me, resting her soft body against my back.*

1139
01:24:17,000 --> 01:24:19,000
You:  "M... Mirari...?"

1140
01:24:19,000 --> 01:24:23,000
Mirari:  "I-I know this isn't much, but... please..."

1141
01:24:23,000 --> 01:24:25,000
*Finally, Mirari speaks.*

1142
01:24:25,000 --> 01:24:32,000
*The next moment, she pulls her body back, and I can instead feel her delicate hands gently rubbing my back.*

1143
01:24:32,000 --> 01:24:38,000
Mirari:  "I do not possess your strength, [player_name]... nor do I share Fuyu's wit or courage."

1144
01:24:38,000 --> 01:24:46,000
Mirari:  "I don't know this side of the mountain well. Even if I {i}did{/i} want to go back home, I wouldn't be of much help."

1145
01:24:46,000 --> 01:24:51,000
Mirari:  "It seems like, no matter what I do... I'm just a nuisance."

1146
01:24:51,000 --> 01:24:55,000
*As Mirari voices her frustration, she begins to rub harder.*

1147
01:24:55,000 --> 01:25:01,000
Mirari:  "That's why, if there's anything I can do, please... don't hesitate to ask."

1148
01:25:01,000 --> 01:25:08,000
Mirari:  "Cooking, cleaning, washing your body for you... If it's something that's within my power, I'll do it."

1149
01:25:08,000 --> 01:25:09,000
You:  "Mirari..."

1150
01:25:09,000 --> 01:25:12,000
*My heart sinks as I contemplate Mirari's words.*

1151
01:25:12,000 --> 01:25:20,000
*Even without knowing the full story behind Mirari's current situation, I'm aware of just how powerless she feels.*

1152
01:25:20,000 --> 01:25:30,000
*In the short time that she's been here, all I've heard from Mirari is how she appreciates what I've done for her, and how she doesn't want to leave.*

1153
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:34,000
*She really isn't making it easy for me to evict her.*

1154
01:25:34,000 --> 01:25:40,000
You:  "Mirari, I'm glad you feel that way, but you really don't need to go this far."

1155
01:25:40,000 --> 01:25:42,000
Mirari:  "..."Go this far"?"

1156
01:25:42,000 --> 01:25:46,000
Mirari:  "I don't understand. All I'm doing is washing your back."

1157
01:25:46,000 --> 01:25:51,000
Mirari:  "Is that strange? Fuyu and I wash one another all the time."

1158
01:25:51,000 --> 01:25:52,000
Mirari:  "Hmm?"

1159
01:25:52,000 --> 01:25:55,000
*Mirari tilts her head with a smile on her face.*

1160
01:25:55,000 --> 01:26:02,000
*It seems that bathing with a near-stranger isn't as extreme of an act for this wolf-girl as it is for me.*

1161
01:26:02,000 --> 01:26:06,000
*(Huh... Maybe bathing together is some kind of half-wolf custom?)*

1162
01:26:06,000 --> 01:26:12,000
*(Just because it isn't common for humans, that doesn't mean there's something weird about it.)*

1163
01:26:12,000 --> 01:26:15,000
You:  "{i}sigh...{/i} Alright. Do as you please."

1164
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:18,000
Mirari:  "Ah... Yes! Thank you very much!"

1165
01:26:18,000 --> 01:26:22,000
You:  "No, you really don't need to go so far as to thank me."

1166
01:26:22,000 --> 01:26:30,000
*Smiling from ear to ear, Mirari picks up a bar of soap, lathers her hands, and begins to rub my back once more.*

1167
01:26:30,000 --> 01:26:37,000
*While she's rubbing my back with her bare hands, I occasionally feel something else slap against my back.*

1168
01:26:37,000 --> 01:26:46,000
*Heavy, but soft. The feeling only lasts for an instant, but it seems like every few seconds, the sensation reappears once more.*

1169
01:26:46,000 --> 01:26:48,000
You:  "S-So Mirari! Uhh..."

1170
01:26:48,000 --> 01:26:51,000
You:  "H-How's life with the rest of your pack?"

1171
01:26:51,000 --> 01:26:53,000
Mirari:  "Hmm? Oh, uhm..."

1172
01:26:53,000 --> 01:26:55,000
Mirari:  "It's fine, I guess."

1173
01:26:55,000 --> 01:26:57,000
*`(If this continues, I...)`*

1174
01:26:57,000 --> 01:26:58,000
You:  "......"

1175
01:26:58,000 --> 01:27:01,000
You:  "Uhm, you and Fuyu seem pretty close."

1176
01:27:01,000 --> 01:27:04,000
You:  "Have you been friends since childhood?"

1177
01:27:04,000 --> 01:27:06,000
Mirari:  "Mmm... In a way."

1178
01:27:06,000 --> 01:27:07,000
You:  "......"

1179
01:27:07,000 --> 01:27:11,000
*(Damn it, Mirari! I'm trying to strike up a conversation here.)*

1180
01:27:11,000 --> 01:27:15,000
*(For whose sake do you think I'm asking these questions?)*

1181
01:27:15,000 --> 01:27:17,000
*Thankfully, before long--*

1182
01:27:17,000 --> 01:27:19,000
Mirari:  "Okay, that ought to do it."

1183
01:27:19,000 --> 01:27:21,000
You:  "Y... You're done?"

1184
01:27:21,000 --> 01:27:25,000
Mirari:  "Uh-huh. Your back and shoulders are all nice and clean."

1185
01:27:25,000 --> 01:27:28,000
Mirari:  "All that's left now is the front."

1186
01:27:28,000 --> 01:27:30,000
*Mirari points between my legs.*

1187
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:32,000
You:  "Oh, right. Let me just--"

1188
01:27:32,000 --> 01:27:33,000
You:  "Wait, what!?"

1189
01:27:33,000 --> 01:27:39,000
Mirari:  "Do you want me to get up and move to your front? Or would you like to turn around?"

1190
01:27:39,000 --> 01:27:42,000
You:  "I'd like to know what the hell's going on!"

1191
01:27:42,000 --> 01:27:48,000
*I quickly cover my crotch with my hands as Mirari starts to squirm around behind my back.*

1192
01:27:48,000 --> 01:27:53,000
Mirari:  "What are you doing, [player_name]? I can't wash your front like this."

1193
01:27:53,000 --> 01:27:55,000
You:  "You don't need to!"

1194
01:27:55,000 --> 01:28:00,000
You:  "Really, you've done enough already. I'll do the front myself, okay?"

1195
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:02,000
*Mirari shakes her head.*

1196
01:28:02,000 --> 01:28:04,000
Mirari:  "That won't do."

1197
01:28:04,000 --> 01:28:10,000
Mirari:  "I said that I would wash you, did I not? I can't just stop half way through."

